{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness","id":1540876,"title":"How would the Technocrat react to the Chronicle of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-21T22:44:17-07:00","id":1540876,"title":"How would the Technocrat react to the Chronicle of Darkness?","content":"Let's assume a building full of Technocrat (25 Mage, 100 Extraordinary Citizen, 500 Sleeper) suddenly find themselves in the Chronicle of Darkness, within a city where every Splat exist. How would the Technocrat react to the various supernatural creature of this new night? Technocrat power are also very diminish, with Arete 5 being the most they could have, and Extraordinary Citizen can only have Max 3 dot in any path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T00:52:51-07:00","id":1540880,"title":"","content":"Research and try to go back.<br /> If not possible then research and continue the mission here.<br /> If they discover the consensus does not work here i guess doing standard power struggles or joining the god machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T01:31:20-07:00","id":1540882,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they seek allies with the Free Council? The Seers of the Throne are far to much like Nephandi, so forget them. The Atlantean Diamond would have little appeal, four dull flavors of Hermetic.<br /> <br /> (I once had all 21 Mage: The Awakening books. Lost them when I lost about nine tenths of my books, never cared to get any of them back). Still a big Mage: The Ascension fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-27-2024, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T10:15:40-07:00","id":1541069,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Seers and the Technocracy: <br /> <br /> 1) On the surface level, the practices they use for effects are very different. In that regard, the Seers will look very much like a mix of Hermetics and Verbena with a sprinkling of other Traditions thrown in. <br /> <br /> 2) Digging deeper the two share a lot of similar approaches to how they manipulate the world and even some overlap in what they want the world to be. They could, in limited circumstances be allies.<br /> <br /> 3) Beneath even that, though, at their core they are greatly opposed. The Technocracy would not at all agree with serving the Exarchs and they are fighting for a world where humanity is free, even if they never realize they are one of the things it needs to be free of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T20:17:17-07:00","id":1541105,"title":"","content":"While I don't know much about the Technocrat, I do know about the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Clam Daeva</b><br /> <b>Technocracy</b>: Most of us don't really care about the Technocracy, they're small in the grand scheme of thing, hostile and not very interesting partner, few might consider them to be a challenge, to lure them out of their order, and into the wild passionate night.<br /> <b>Iteration X</b>: Ignorable people, they're too focus on their machinery to be any fun for the Daeva, even to those who like people like this.<br /> <b><b>N.W.O</b></b><b>.</b>: The Daeva like to play with this Convention the most, using mind game and love trick to make these so call &quot;police&quot; fall head over heel for them.<br /> <b>Progenitor</b>: They may be able to heal their body, but they can't heal from heartbreak, and the Daeva like to have fun breaking a few heart.<br /> <b>Syndicate</b>: Heartless money grabber, but they would make a great sugar parent, just discard them when the benefit run out, like they do with their credit card.<br /> <b>Void Engineer</b>: The most alluring of the Convention, but also the hardest to reach, but any Daeva who get a Void Engineer to be their lover is a lucky corpse.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Gangrel</b><br /> <b>Technocracy</b>: A bunch of technological freak, with no real survival skill outside of their concrete jungle, strip of their fancy toys, they're are still mortal.<br /> <b>Iteration X</b>: The most tech reliant of the Technocracy, they're puny of flesh and vile of blood, don't waste your time on them, unless they try to start a fight with the Beast.<br /> <b>N.W.O.</b>: They're the least reliant on fancy gadget, but all they do is watch, as their friend face get eaten.<br /> <b>Progenitor</b>: Disgusting, what they create are mere mockery of our power, but their blood and flesh are more potent than most.<br /> <b>Syndicate</b>: Rich bastard, they live their live without knowing true wisdom and pain, just a growl is all it take to scare these mortal to their secure home.<br /> <b>Void Engineer</b>: Let them look toward the star, while the earth beneath them crumble.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Mekhet</b><br /> <b>Technocracy</b>: They're well verse in the art of surveillance, but they're small in number, and clueless to the our way, this is our key to learning their secret.<br /> <b>Iteration X</b>: Their machine body poision their blood, best watch from afar, their only worth is their machine part, so savage them if you find one dead.<br /> <b>N.W.O.</b>: Hide deeper in the shadow around these technocrat, before you strike and suck out all of their secret.<br /> <b>Progenitor</b>: For the amount of knowlegde that they possesses, it's almost worth the horror that come with it, almost.<br /> <b>Syndicate</b>: Why do they act like they're so important? I can't find their name in any company.<br /> <b>Void Engineer</b>: I'm not convince that what they say lie beyond our earth is true, but I can't seem to find any evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Nosferatu</b><br /> <b>Technocracy</b>: What do they even want with us? If you find one, give them a reason as to why they shouldn't mess with us.<br /> <b>Iteration X</b>: They kind of creep me out, those machine part shouldn't be possible.<br /> <b>N.W.O.</b>: They need to keep their eye to themselves, or they might see something that will make those eye never close again.<br /> <b>Progenitor</b>: I think they could lessen our curse, but I they will do it, with or without our consent to do that.<br /> <b>Syndicate</b>: Their nightmare are so shallow, but their pocket are deep, so be careful when you meet one.<br /> <b>Void Enginneer</b>: What they see, beyond this sky, couldn't that bad, could it?<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Venture</b><br /> <b>Technocracy</b>: Be envious of their knowledge, be wary of their mind, but crush them when they borther you all the same.<br /> <b>Iteration X</b>: Aren't machine suppose to follow order? So why don't you follow my.<br /> <b>N.W.O.</b>: Think they know inside a person mind, their technique are mere trick compare to our discipline.<br /> <b>Progenitor</b>: Their blood is highly prize among us, they can make animal blood taste divine, but they could poision that very same vein.<br /> <b>Void Engineer</b>: Great servant if you want to go to space, but why would you, when all that matter is here on earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T15:37:00-07:00","id":1541141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541105#post1541105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't know much about the Technocrat, I do know about the Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do need to understand the Union if you want to know how others will react to them.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is, above all else, the Conspiracy. They're masters in the same game as vampires, even if with some differences in focus.<br /> <br /> Chronicles is a setting characterized by a Do What You Will state. The Union come from a place of rampant paranoia. It is made of secrets, manipulation and caution.<br /> <br /> Finally, even limited to Arete 5 they are stupidly dangerous. This is more than enough to do a lot of things, if you keep the idea of them having access to their kind of magic while in the CoD universe.<br /> <br /> A vampire with any knowledge of their existence, yet with such obnoxious superiority complex, is soon to be a dead vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T18:32:14-07:00","id":1541313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1540880#post1540880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Research and try to go back.<br /> If not possible then research and continue the mission here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. That's what they would do.<br /> <br /> First order of the day would be survive. Protect themselves. Study the environment. 25 Enlightened personnel is not enough to wage war on the world. Their first direct would be to find safe heaven, than study the environment. And then, expand. Recruit. They'll need help from the locals - which does NOT include the &quot;Reality Deviants&quot;. Those are the enemies.<br /> <br /> They'll seek to get more sleepers into their schemes, indoctrinate new Extraordinary Citizens and when possible, recruit new &quot;Mages&quot;, as long as they manage to induce these new and strange &quot;enlightened&quot; individuals into their worldviews.<br /> <br /> From that point forward, their goal would be to infiltrate and expand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they discover the consensus does not work here i guess doing standard power struggles or joining the god machine. </div> </div> </div>I highly doubt they would join the God Machine.<br /> <br /> It would take them a very, very long time to learn Consensus doesn't work, since they'll be in no position to test their social engineering methods that would allow them to attest that.<br /> <br /> Therefore, power struggles would be the order of the day, once they consider themselves adjusted enough to their new reality.<br /> <br /> Such a group of Technocrats would actually be highly dangerous and could represent a serious threat to all the rest of the splats. Technocrats are master conspirators and massively paranoid, and their, let's call it &quot;work ethos&quot; is something that practically doesn't exist in Chronicles. They have a rigid Hierarchy and equally rigid goals but are highly adaptive, meaning they would work towards achieving global relevance like a bunch of zealots and brothers in arms.<br /> <br /> I'm not kidding, there could be a big chance that they would achieve the post of &quot;alpha dogs&quot; in this world in relatively short time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T20:40:22-07:00","id":1541321,"title":"","content":"Well, they would still have to compete against the thousand of other Conspiracy existing in Chronicle, and some of them make actual Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T01:07:06-07:00","id":1541324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541321#post1541321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they would still have to compete against the thousand of other Conspiracy existing in Chronicle, and some of them make actual Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but if they have their powers, then they have a lot they can do. And they would probably be making their own Deviants in short notice, as making and altering people in labs is their thing anyways.<br /> <br /> I personally wouldn't say so fast that they would become a top dog, not even am I sure they would refuse to work with the monsters. It depends a lot on who they are exactly and how things happen in practice.<br /> <br /> However it happens, though, the Union will try to gather as much information as possible while giving none. They'll try to embed agents everywhere, and they have their powers to make it work. They'll gather resources and build safe places.<br /> <br /> And they're well trained and conditioned. They watch each other for signs of compromise. They never let their guard down as a group.<br /> <br /> What may be a problem for them in this new reality is actually that their resistance to work with others and too rigid thinking may end up putting them against more enemies than they need to have.<br /> <br /> They're likely to start any interaction with any group with an almost hostile attitude from the get go, and that means the local supernatural community has the upper hand to organize and deal with them if and when they become a problem. On their native reality this kind of mutual coexistence is virtually unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T04:13:30-07:00","id":1541327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541321#post1541321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they would still have to compete against the thousand of other Conspiracy existing in Chronicle, and some of them make actual Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but so too does the Technocracy makes Deviants of their own.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy also started small, probably no much bigger than that lost group. And they managed to pretty much &quot;conquer the world&quot; in a relatively short time (just a few centuries). And in the World of Darkness, they did it from the ground up, they initially didn't have the organization and modus operandi that the modern Technocracy have.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, it is internal bickering and bureocracy that constraints their actions more than their capabilities. Personal agendas and egos get in the way of the mission.<br /> <br /> This group however would have a clean slate and a mindset of &quot;barbarians at the gate&quot; to push them towards success and towards keeping unity.<br /> <br /> Their unity by the way has always been the key to their astonishing success, even thou it is not perfect it is still miles ahead of any other group.<br /> <br /> Besides, all other splats had their own little feuds and internal divisions, and that's what allowed their meteoric rise - which is also something present in Chronicles.<br /> <br /> It's like in Ecology, invasive species quickly become dominant in a new environment because all other species in a location are already under dynamic balance, so when an alien species comes, it offsets that balance.<br /> <br /> These Technocrats would have the same effect, spreading throughout the cracks in the system like a plague of locusts.<br /> <br /> To begin with, in Chronicles just like as in WoD, despite these &quot;conspiracies of the Dark&quot; being global, their actual power is localized. You basically have decentralized power bases of monsters that are centered around cities, even if each one these locations adhere to larger geographic hierarchies.<br /> <br /> Now, 25 Enlightened Technocrats, 100 Extraordinary Citizens and 500 employed sleepers, is more than enough to granting &quot;control&quot; over at least a medium sized city. Now, I don't mean that this means completely wiping out all the Reality Deviants of said city, far from it and quite the opposite actually, doing that would be actually stupid. What I mean is that these numbers are enough manpower to granting a safe base of operations, resources to maintain their operations and capabilities to keep track on everything happening on their domain. And that also implies the capabilities to keep track of the movements of the Reality Deviants on their domain.<br /> <br /> From that point on, they would start their process of expansion. Setting 101 Rooms to recruit the strange &quot;Enlightened&quot; people of this reality - basically brainwashing centers to turn captured Mages into brand new Enlightened Technocrats. Centers for formation of Extraordinary Citizens.<br /> <br /> One way they could go about, for example: setting shop in a medium sized city.<br /> <br /> Then, rather than making a move on their location, they set up investigation throughout 3 dozens of OTHER medium sized cities across the globe - preferably even in other states or nations.<br /> <br /> Why? Because they don't want to attract attention.<br /> <br /> After monitoring things for a while, they identify their targets. Their main objective is to kidnap Mages for brainwashing into new agents.<br /> <br /> They'll go for the easier targets, for the &quot;low hanging fruits&quot;, not to powerful &quot;archmages&quot;, but rather to newbies. That doesn't matter, they'll have time to improve and even better, will be less resilient towards indoctrination.<br /> <br /> These 36 other cities that their small group is monitoring will be connected with their main &quot;fortress&quot; with the use of Correspondence Portals and Gates. Entropy will help them pick and choose their targets.<br /> <br /> In case anyone of their &quot;monitoring stations&quot; gets too hot, they just drop it altogether and set up a new one.<br /> <br /> For all the other splats, it would be like a &quot;ghost in the machine&quot;. It's one Mage disappearing here, another one over there... Things that actually are common in the world.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, they'll be working towards gaining localized mundane power (money and political and societal influence), but also striving to doing that over other locations too - and on many times, geographically disconnected locations - for example, acquiring businesses in Mexico, Chile, Angola and Belgium. On occasions, they would starting spreading their tendrils over places they are actively monitoring, but in others they would just simply set remote businesses without active surveillance, just for the sake of redundancy and future expansion.<br /> <br /> Then, after a few rounds of that dance, they would acquire enough Intel and enough knowledge of the local Reality Deviants that they would feel comfortable to expand their bases of operations towards another city, after gathering Intel and amassing enough manpower.<br /> <br /> Their main constraint would be Enlightened personnel; so that would be their focal point, identifying Mages and indoctrinating them. Which is why they would set that web of &quot;surveillance cities&quot; connected with Correspondence with their main &quot;fortress city&quot;, for the main purpose of identifying and &quot;acquiring&quot; new recruits.<br /> <br /> But once they do gather sufficient manpower, they would make a move towards fortifying the next city as a new stronghold.<br /> <br /> Rinse and repeat, rinse and repeat, until they manage to acquire enough power to set up for higher things - say, they completely dominate an area equal to a state or medium sized nation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they would prefer to utterly dominate a small nation, thus allowing a higher degree of control over a small geographic location. They could easily dominate Uruguay for instance, or Nicaragua, or Yemen or any other, doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Then they would start to move over the food chain. That would perhaps become the point upon which they start their Pogrom. Their position from &quot;silent observers&quot; working in the shadows would switch to active hunters, to ensure their complete dominance and security over their holdings.<br /> <br /> From that point forward, they would set out to accomplish their mission. Outside of their domains, they would keep their job of &quot;silent observers&quot; working in the shadows, gathering Intel and spreading their tendrils, with the purpose of setting the stage for new acquisitions.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's not so different from what the Technocratic Union did in the World of Darkness. In fact, it is pretty much EXACTLY what they did. And the other splats were unable to stop them because those others were already under a &quot;dynamic balance&quot;, countering each other, thus being unable to deal with an external threat.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats go to a new location en masse, focusing their resources.<br /> <br /> I'm telling you, this small group of Technocrats might not seem much, but they would actually pose a serious threat to everybody else in due time.<br /> <br /> And what's a few centuries to them? They have time and patience to fulfill their job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T05:28:34-07:00","id":1541328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541327#post1541327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>That is all very highly improbable.<br /> <br /> First of all, CofD is better at intergating new faction into it power balance.<br /> <br /> Secondly, at what sphere could Ascension Mage open portal between different city?<br /> <br /> Third, when the Technocracy start to kidnap Awaken Mage, the Pentacle and Seer of the Throne will be on their trail, and Seer of the Throne have much better control and knowledge of CofD than the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Fourth, other supernatural being would find them, there're simply no way that they can hide forever, especially from the God Machine, and various other Splat that have very good locating abilities.<br /> <br /> Fifth, they would still have power struggle, it the human nature, and the Technocrat are still human.<br /> <br /> Sixth, how would the Technocrat do all of that, when they technically don't exist in CofD? It would be very awkard for them to go open a bank account or get a job, when they technically don't live anywhere in CofD earth.<br /> <br /> Seveth, they would still have to battle the Contagion, which would mess with their power even more than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T12:51:52-07:00","id":1541351,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> that's a very narrow view of the CoD, and an inaccurate understanding of invasive species or how they serve as an analogy. There's indeed some advantage for the Union in being an unknown quantity, but this new environment is unknown to them, too.<br /> <br /> One thing you're failing to consider is that while it is our world on the surface, the humanity from CoD differs deeply from both RL and from WoD. The whole ecosystem they form with the supernatural around them is starkly distinct, and the Union won't be immediately prepared to understand, respond to or use that.<br /> <br /> But I think the greatest problem is the premise that they would boost their numbers with local Mages.<br /> <br /> Regardless of mechanical similarities as an RPG, Mages from each world are completely different things. They're not interchangeable, the whole premises and metaphysics behind them are worlds apart.<br /> <br /> There's zero reason to think the Technocrats can booster their numbers at all, at least at the Enlightened level. They can co-opt local man power, but those will work within local parameters, something again that the Union doesn't have a lot of understanding to begin with.<br /> <br /> It's easier for them to form alliances with local &quot;RDs&quot; than to find a way to incorporate how the locals work within the Union's framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 09-01-2024, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T13:16:43-07:00","id":1541353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541328#post1541328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secondly, at what sphere could Ascension Mage open portal between different city?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>3rd, which is accessible at character creation in Ascension. In fact, even among NPCs a character with less than that is barely considered a proper Mage. Unless this group is specifically made of training newbies, it's likely that most of them have Arete 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> So the likelihood of a portal maker among them is almost 100%.<br /> <br /> Hiding in exceedingly efficient ways, making new identities from scratch and literally brainwashing themselves to ensure complete loyalty is also par of the course for them, it's literally the three things you expect from any cadet that finished basic training.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that dominating the setting would be far from as simple as Magus Maximus said, but at the same time you're falling in the simplest, most naive error: you're trying to talk about a group you admittedly don't know very well.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is <b>the Conspiracy</b>, it is their whole shtick. The Illuminati, the Men in Black, the Government Above the Government. Each Convention represents an archetypal super conspiracy. Science is their favorite tool, but their game is secret domination.<br /> <br /> Yes, they are out of their turf, and they have no guarantee of success in this situation, not just because that's their literary device. But you do need to understand this trope to understand how they work, and what are their strong suits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T13:51:24-07:00","id":1541356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541328#post1541328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is all very highly improbable.<br /> <br /> First of all, CofD is better at intergating new faction into it power balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. The way that the Technocracy was built was to dominate the setting. Their structure is pretty unique.<br /> <br /> Besides, it is like I said, they would be like an invasive species entering a new habitat. You have the local species competing with one another and balancing each other out, when the foreign element is introduced it offsets said balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, at what sphere could Ascension Mage open portal between different city? </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 4. Not an uncommon feat and not uncommon for them to do so. With Corr 3 they can already teleport. From a group of 25 of them, even if they are fresh recruits, you can expect at least a few of them to have such capacity at the get go.<br /> <br /> But that's just an example, and not even needed. They can set a small camp of Extraordinary Citizens and Sleepers to watch out different locations and proceed with &quot;manual extraction&quot;. That wouldn't be a problem for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third, when the Technocracy start to kidnap Awaken Mage, the Pentacle and Seer of the Throne will be on their trail, and Seer of the Throne have much better control and knowledge of CofD than the Technocracy. </div> </div> </div>You're not really analysing things properly. Don't imagine car chases left and right and basically open war. We are talking about a slow, methodic and careful process that would occur over the span of years and upon unconnected geographic locations. A rate of one kidnapped Mage per year is feasible, within their capabilities and low profile enough to not attract too much undesired attention. Imagine that these Technocrats set a base of operations in Hanoi Vietnam, then in 2025 a Mage goes missing in Beijing, than in 2026 another one in Detroit, than in 2027 yet another in Mecca and so on - and I'm citing major cities just to explain, so I'm using well know cities, but this would most likely be done on medium sized cities instead of major urban centers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth, other supernatural being would find them, there're simply no way that they can hide forever, especially from the God Machine, and various other Splat that have very good locating abilities. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But perhaps not. They'll initially lay very, very low. You won't see anyone of that group doing anything for a good while - not anything obvious. And not anything that warrants bigger attention from the top dogs, until it is basically too late and they are well established and entrenched.<br /> <br /> They are not vampires, so they don't need to feed. They are not werewolves or other beasts, so they don't care about the weird &quot;spirits&quot; they'll find in that place.<br /> <br /> Initially, they would confine themselves to acquiring monetary means, then local political influence, and monitoring their places of interest (the city upon which they set up shop, the cities around them and other places around the globe, for both redundancy, safe escape and potential future gains)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fifth, they would still have power struggle, it the human nature, and the Technocrat are still human. </div> </div> </div>That's not a concern while they are still small however. That becomes problematic once they grow too much. Initially, they'll have a shared goal, a strict hierarchy and most importantly, the need to survive. Their little conspiracy is their best hope to survive for any individual.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy have the best hierarchy in the WoD, hence why they are so successful. Those lost Technocrats wouldn't have the structure of the Union, but they would share the same mentality and the same modus operandi.<br /> <br /> If you understood how the Technocracy works, you would understand why these guys can be potentially so dangerous in such a setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sixth, how would the Technocrat do all of that, when they technically don't exist in CofD? It would be very awkard for them to go open a bank account or get a job, when they technically don't live anywhere in CofD earth. </div> </div> </div>That's the easiest part. In fact, being legally non existent is a boon for them. All they need to do is brainwash/indoctrinate some &quot;sleepers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's say they appear somewhere in the middle of the night at a farm somewhere in South Africa.<br /> <br /> Well, the first thing they'll do would be to subdue the farmer and his family and brainwash them. Now they have their very first rudimentary base of operations and access to the farmer's monetary base.<br /> <br /> From there, they would try to use their credit cards, access their own documents over the internet and learn they don't legally exist.<br /> <br /> The next step then would be to visit every other farms in the region and brainwash their owners too.<br /> <br /> And then, carefully expand from that. I won't detail every single small step, but it ain't that complicate.<br /> <br /> And their Syndicate members are masters of finances. They know how to grow money in inconspicuous ways - for example, setting different businesses that never communicate between one another in any way.<br /> <br /> Then they travel to South America and brainwash some other common folk at some forgotten corner and establish yet another base of businesses that have no obvious connection with their farms in South Africa except for the fact that they serve the same masters.<br /> <br /> And on and on.<br /> <br /> And in here, Entropy 1 and Correspondence 1 are the key Spheres. Entropy 1 alone turns the process of acquiring targets almost trivial.<br /> <br /> Now, let's do some math here: 25 new Mages in 25 years doubles their numbers. And in 100 years, that's 125 Enlightened Technocrats ready to establish the organization. That may seem small, but it actually isn't.<br /> <br /> From that they can start to plan for higher flights.<br /> <br /> And the more time passes, the more capable they'll become and better they'll understand the world around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seveth, they would still have to battle the Contagion, which would mess with their power even more than usual. </div> </div> </div>Sure, this is a problem, as is the God Machine.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats however have several protocols for the containment of threats. For instance, they work by setting off independent cells. In the WoD, they have faced cataclysmic events and have been contaminated by eldritch menaces. But none of that ever broke them down. And those &quot;contaminations&quot; happened due to their sheer size - they are, after all, the bigger dogs around in the WoD.<br /> <br /> For instance, the Syndicate has been infiltrated by Pentex, which if you don't know are a bunch of cultists that worship an eldritch manifestation of destruction whose purpose is to destroy the world.<br /> <br /> That hasn't been unnoticed thou, and it is been contained albeit slowly. And the reason for that slow take is due to many internal politics that are a consequence of their size rather than their capabilities - in theory they could wipe out said &quot;contamination&quot; in an instant, but they don't because of internal conflicts of interests.<br /> <br /> Basically, in the WoD they are the biggest and meanest dog out there, therefore their internal interests are more important than external threats, which in their view are only &quot;minor inconveniences&quot;.<br /> <br /> That wouldn't be the case however for a small group of lost Technocrats.<br /> <br /> Besides, they are great at gathering information - this is one of their main things. They'll be quick to extract Intel from any one splats that they come in contact with.<br /> <br /> Of special notice would be those groups that oppose the God Machine. As soon as the Technocrats start learning about this threat, it is very possible that they could forge alliances with said groups - and perhaps, even integrating these into the fold.<br /> <br /> If they actually manage to achieve that, this would not only prove to be a major source of valuable Intel about this world but they could also structure these groups into much more effective and functional structures.<br /> <br /> So yes, not only does these Technocrats have great potential for expansion but they can also learn how to work with the hand that they have and exploit the cracks in the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 09-01-2024, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T14:52:24-07:00","id":1541362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541351#post1541351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> that's a very narrow view of the CoD, and an inaccurate understanding of invasive species or how they serve as an analogy. There's indeed some advantage for the Union in being an unknown quantity, but this new environment is unknown to them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is an unknown environment. Which is why they would carefully analyse it before making any move. The best you can hope for the very first decades would be for them to bind together a small network, only big enough for them to be able to set up shop, therefore just a small operation (their size is small after all) with enough monetary means for them to sustain themselves, and then just enough to build a surveillance network upon whichever points of interest they determine.<br /> <br /> Then, they would sit out and listen. Until they found out their first vampires.<br /> <br /> Then they would investigate those thoroughly. Associates, common routes, connections.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later they would encounter the other splats, one by one. Watching from the distance, and disappearing as soon as they fear for any signs of exposure.<br /> <br /> This alone would take decades.<br /> <br /> And this time would give them the basic framework of how things work, and allow them to plan accordingly and to adapt.<br /> <br /> Then they would begin to feel a bit more secure to take more active measures. Kidnapping and &quot;interviewing&quot; the &quot;locals&quot;, and thus getting Intel in a more direct manner, but always done with selected low risk targets, over extended periods of time and across great distances.<br /> <br /> That way, they can gather a ton of valuable Intel and understanding of the rules of the game they're playing, while remaining largely inconspicuous.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing you're failing to consider is that while it is our world on the surface, the humanity from CoD differs deeply from both RL and from WoD. The whole ecosystem they form with the supernatural around them is starkly distinct, and the Union won't be immediately prepared to understand, respond to or use that.<br /> <br /> But I think the greatest problem is the premise that they would boost their numbers with local Mages.<br /> <br /> Regardless of mechanical similarities as an RPG, Mages from each world are completely different things. They're not interchangeable, the whole premises and metaphysics behind them are worlds apart.<br /> <br /> There's zero reason to think the Technocrats can booster their numbers at all, at least at the Enlightened level. They can co-opt local man power, but those will work within local parameters, something again that the Union doesn't have a lot of understanding to begin with. </div> </div> </div>Well, these Technocrats would operate on the basis of what they understand. That would depend on what they understand of as &quot;Mages&quot; in the CoD. They may even recognize that these &quot;Mages&quot; are somewhat different, but conclude that they nonetheless operate within a similar framework.<br /> <br /> Thus meaning that they could conclude that they could potentially induce these &quot;Mages&quot; as potential &quot;Enlightened&quot; pool - even if they need at the end to admit that those represent a &quot;new/alternative type of Enlightenment&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's easier for them to form alliances with local &quot;RDs&quot; than to find a way to incorporate how the locals work within the Union's framework. </div> </div> </div>While I do agree that they could be open to such alliances, I don't believe for a second they would simply resign to being junior partners to other groups and most importantly, completely abandoning their mission of protecting the Masses.<br /> <br /> While it may be difficult, they would try to boost their manpower in terms of &quot;supernatural mojo&quot; (mundane power is important, but supernatural mojo is also essential for their purposes).<br /> <br /> I don't discard the possibility of them to adapt and forego the Damian rules, and start to actively &quot;recruit&quot; &quot;Reality Deviants&quot;, preferably by means of deep brainwashing. I believe they would prefer to do it with the Mages of the setting, due to them still being &quot;human&quot; instead of supernatural beasts, but if as you say they would conclude that &quot;it's not the same&quot; (which I don't fully agree), then I don't discard them turning towards &quot;Cyber Vampires&quot; to boost their ranks.<br /> <br /> And again, I don't agree that they couldn't recruit local Mages.\u200b Free Council and Apostates for instance could become a good recruiting pool, and some you may not even need to brainwash, just convince to join. I do not see that as beyond the realm of possibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree with you that dominating the setting would be far from as simple as Magus Maximus said </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is simple by any stretch of the imagination, but I believe it is feasible. Not something that would occur over night however - in that aspect, I need to remind you that the very Technocracy in the WoD had a very similar trajectory, and they weren't as trained at the begin as these individuals would be. But it took them a few centuries to achieve their current position, so yes, I do believe that given a few centuries, they could emerge on top here too. A slow process of incremental gains, but it is absolutely feasible. Not guaranteed, but possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T16:52:00-07:00","id":1541366,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a>, feasible is different from certain, that's the distinction you're failing to make. It's certainly feasible, and I think you're mostly right about their method. We do need to consider the challenges and obstacles, though.<br /> <br /> One of the big first obstacle is the need to survive without the Union. Regardless of how similar this world is to theirs, they are indeed stranded in an alien environment. That may force their hand, and they may be got by some native org because they do start in a weakened position.<br /> <br /> The environment, specially the supernatural one, is dynamic, which means that their expertise in hiding doesn't automatically means they're out of danger. And it is made worse by this world being even more dynamic in this regard. The supernatural beings of this world also have resources they're not used to, even if compared with their apparent counterparts.<br /> <br /> Union agents are exceptional at hiding, but local Mages are also exceptional at finding stuff, and do so through means the Union never heard about. In general CoD splats are better at finding out things. This is one of many examples of risks the Union is completely unprepared to deal with at first, and this first is crucial.<br /> <br /> About the distinction on Mages, how the Technocrats think they work is irrelevant. The distinction is a fact. I'm not saying they can't use technological props, I'm saying they're a distinct splat altogether, whose powers have zero to do with Ascension's magic. Local Mages don't work on belief, and their Paradox doesn't come from Reality lashing out. A local Mage that stop believing in the Supernal simply stops doing magic until they stop their deluded nonsense.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of similar results achieved through completely unrelated methods. And we have to add that those people do achieve similar results, so they're not strangers to mind control. The Union never got to brainwash RDs without being noticed, that won't start now.<br /> <br /> Now, can they recruit people to their cause? Absolutely. It just isn't as straightforward as indoctrinating fellow Enlightened (which already isn't all that straightforward), and the distinction does add to the complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T19:57:50-07:00","id":1541377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541356#post1541356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your first point of Technocracy being bulit to dominate the setting is true for World of Darkness but not Chronicle, and it structure aren't that unique in CofD.<br /> <br /> I think you need to stop comparing organization to species, there're balance sure, but when something offset the balance the balance try to bring the new thing down, and either the new thing die, or it become part of the balance. Sometime the new thing win, but not when there isn't much support for it.<br /> <br /> What does manual extraction mean? And when they set up camp in other city, no matter how small would still be detected by some supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> Still a kidnap mage is still a kidnap mage, if the city have any local pentacle or ministry they would still be interested in seeing where the mage went, especially if it a newly awaken one, which all awakening mage can detect when they're awaken. And sympathethic mage is a thing.<br /> <br /> They will be spotted, certainly from the God Machine, I mean they're a dimensional anomaly that can bend reality to fit their vision, that almost the same as the Contagion, and when the God Machine notice, the angle will flock down, and the demon and the stigmatic will notice, and then the Sworn and False will notice.<br /> <br /> If they do use that brainwashing method, other supernatural will know, in CofD many &quot;mortal&quot; have some kind of supernatural merit, some more than other, and if they would also have to battle against the Hunter who outnumbered them by the ten of thousand. Especially the one with more technological ties such as TFV or the V.S.C.U.<br /> <br /> The Contagion doesn't care how small or big you're and if the Mage of CofD have problem with the Contagion messing with their power, I don't think the Technocrat have it any better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T14:54:39-07:00","id":1541410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541377#post1541377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Contagion doesn't care how small or big you're and if the Mage of CofD have problem with the Contagion messing with their power, I don't think the Technocrat have it any better.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason for their powers to be affected at all by the Contagion, even <b>if </b>the Contagion is a big thing, which is a dire assumption in itself.<br /> <br /> If you want them to have their original powers working in the CoD, stick to it. They reshape reality. I don't see any way in which the Contagion would impede or affect this kind of power. It is as alien to the Contagion as it is to everything else.<br /> <br /> By the way, they don't attract the Abyss, either. Their power doesn't care about the Supernal, it doesn't reach through the Abyss, it stays completely in the mundane world, changing its very laws.<br /> <br /> Ascension's Paradox is far less of a problem than Awakening's, and in fact it is even uncertain if any form of Paradox would affect the Technocrats at all. This world has no Consensus to push against their work.<br /> <br /> Unless you made this exercise only to boast about the CoD, your premise has some logical consequences that must be accounted for, and not everything is bad news to the aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T17:29:02-07:00","id":1541421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541410#post1541410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no reason for their powers to be affected at all by the Contagion, even <b>if </b>the Contagion is a big thing, which is a dire assumption in itself.<br /> <br /> If you want them to have their original powers working in the CoD, stick to it. They reshape reality. I don't see any way in which the Contagion would impede or affect this kind of power. It is as alien to the Contagion as it is to everything else.<br /> <br /> By the way, they don't attract the Abyss, either. Their power doesn't care about the Supernal, it doesn't reach through the Abyss, it stays completely in the mundane world, changing its very laws.<br /> <br /> Ascension's Paradox is far less of a problem than Awakening's, and in fact it is even uncertain if any form of Paradox would affect the Technocrats at all. This world has no Consensus to push against their work.<br /> <br /> Unless you made this exercise only to boast about the CoD, your premise has some logical consequences that must be accounted for, and not everything is bad news to the aliens.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Contagion does reshape reality, it probably will affect the Technocrat power. And there is no reason to assume that the Contagion can't affect being that come from another dimension, the Contagion already kind does affect other dimension stuff. Also why wouldn't their power be affected by the Contagion? Contagion can mess with spirit stuff so they could mess with the Technocrat Avatar.<br /> <br /> Since there is no Consensus, the Technocrat power come from the Avatar that is within them, which definetly can be affected, since Avatar is a type of spirit if I can remember. While they wouldn't get Paradox because there is no Consensus, reality could still punish them since they mess with the Occult Physic that make up reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T04:54:42-07:00","id":1541440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541421#post1541421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> why wouldn't their power be affected?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that would require further assumptions, which is a stretch of the proposed exercise. For the Contagion to affect them, a new function of the Contagion must be added. For this reality to punish them, a new property of this reality must be added.<br /> <br /> The Contagion is quite optional to begin with, and hardly a common happenstance. It isn't a default relevant obstacle in comparisons between CoD's splats, why would it be relevant here? If it is, then Occam's Razor dictates the path of least assumptions, and that's that the Technocrats aren't likely to face it or to be significantly affected.<br /> <br /> Even if they are, they'll just adapt. And it is already a stretch that they're not affected by the very nature of reality (i.e. their powers work as normal), but are by a disease proper to this reality. Also that this reality can't impede their powers, but somehow can punish them for using it when the very phenomenon that does it doesn't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T05:41:37-07:00","id":1541524,"title":"","content":"I didn't suggest that they would brainwash Mages to forget the Supernal, that much the techies would learn pretty fast. But they still could be brainwashed into &quot;the mission&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yes, voluntary recruiting may be better.<br /> <br /> Now, the absence of Consensus is, indeed, massive. If they are immune to Paradox and Permadox, then they become a behemoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T06:00:32-07:00","id":1541526,"title":"","content":"I just remembered, there is an alternative, or perhaps a complement in order for them to boost their ranks with &quot;legit&quot; techies. But it is far harder to achieve and not necessarily available at the get go.<br /> <br /> First of all, there is the use of a Principia, a tome of knowledge used for awakening people. Since those 100 Except Citizens and 500 Sleepers should have Avatars, and thus eligible for WoD Awakenings (rather than CoD Awakening).<br /> <br /> The problem is that building such an item requires Prime 5 if I'm not mistaken.<br /> <br /> Then, assuming that CoD sleepers do NOT have Avatars (which is almost certainly the case), then the Techies can still grow people on tubes... And create real Avatars for them.<br /> <br /> Then, they could Awaken the Avatars of these clones using the Principia.<br /> <br /> The problem with this is that, besides the Principia, it needs at least 1 Technocrat with Life 5, Mind 5 and Dimensional Science 5, which is no small amount of &quot;technical expertise&quot;. But it is doable.<br /> <br /> If no one of the 25 techies possess that amount of knowledge at the start, it is still possible that at least one could reach that level, but it would obviously take quite some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T16:22:59-07:00","id":1541550,"title":"","content":"I think it would be ST territory to say that growing an Avatar would be possible. Depending on how we look at it, since local humans have CoD Souls instead of Avatars, using Spirit would just create such a soul instead of an Avatar.<br /> <br /> But yes, at least the Citizens brought would be potential stock for new Enlightened. And hey, if the lab-grown humans aren't able to achieve Enlightenment, then they can Awaken to the Supernal, at least.<br /> <br /> Given an arbitrarily long time, and assuming they're not impeded by others, the Union can have at least some lab-grown Mages of one kind or another.<br /> <br /> Lets just be clear to those who don't know this stuff: by no means we're talking mass production or even a reliable output of Major splats. It takes a lot to grow humans in a lab, and then they're just as equipped as anyone else to Awaken. So most, and I mean most, won't.<br /> <br /> Principia help, but they're not exactly on <i>reliable </i>territory, otherwise WoD would be a very different place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T18:39:11-07:00","id":1541553,"title":"","content":"In CofD lab grown human could turn out to be either a Deviant (who can't awaken) or a Promethean (who can't awaken before they finish their pilgrimage, which can't be speed up with magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T18:59:13-07:00","id":1541554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541553#post1541553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In CofD lab grown human could turn out to be either a Deviant (who can't awaken) or a Promethean (who can't awaken before they finish their pilgrimage, which can't be speed up with magic).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. If the Technocrats have their powers working, then it's perfectly doable. Growing a normal human in a lab just takes Life, Mind and Spirit, with optional Prime or Matter.<br /> <br /> By the way, Deviants and Prometheans are the results of specific processes, they're not standard for &quot;lab-grown human&quot;. I'm not even sure if CoD Mages really can't make humans with magic, but regardless, Technocrats can and do, regularly. It takes quite a toll in resources, though, so this group would have to be more conservative for a time.<br /> <br /> Oh, I forgot to ask earlier, how would they get Quintessence in your exercise? Is it impossible to get, possible to harvest, are there Nodes, or would they be able to use Mana in place of Quint?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T19:04:32-07:00","id":1541556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541554#post1541554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I forgot to ask earlier, how would they get Quintessence in your exercise? Is it impossible to get, possible to harvest, are there Nodes, or would they be able to use Mana in place of Quint?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're able to get Quintessence from the same source as the Awakening Mage. But it would require the Technocrat to use Prime to convert Mana into Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T06:23:35-07:00","id":1541572,"title":"","content":"First, to contextualize the matter, since a technocratic building appeared in CofD, I'm going to assume that it was magic. In this case, this would put the building in its place, but it wouldn't attract the attention of ordinary people. However, it would attract the attention of the creatures of darkness, after all, a new player in the city. The Technocrats would try to do two things: first, get information about where they are, what happened and what has changed; second, get resources, after all, they are now in a new environment, deprived of contacts and far from any source of income they had before. Soon, they would be called to the attention of the other creatures of darkness who would knock on their door. Some of them might send a scout first, but eventually they would make a direct intervention. I believe that 4 species would be the main interested parties: vampires, mages, arisen (mummies) and beasts, the latter being less likely, It would all depend on how many and how much influence they had within the city.<br /> <br /> Depending on the group or intentions of these creatures, they could sabotage the technocrats or even exterminate the group as a last resort, perhaps even joining forces to do so, but I'll assume that the factions present are not of the shoot first, ask questions later type. The kindred would be interested in their abilities so they would be start an partnership and the technocrats wouldn't be in a position to refuse; the mages I think would start with something similar to a non-aggression pact, both sides don't know what to expect from the other yet, considering that they still don't know how the other's magic works; the arisen I don't see then wanting to have peaceful relations with the technocrats unless in the case where he abandoned his judge, but whatever the case I believe they would avoid direct combat against an unknown enemy, so they seek information first and then take action, either to destroy them or use them, in the last case they may judge that they are more trouble than it would be worth; The beasts I think would ignore it, unless a particularly powerful one had influence in the city, in which case he could offer an alliance or a deal like the one offered be the kindred. As for the other creatures, I believe that the existence of the Technocracy would interfere little in their lives. The lost would continue to flee, the created would remain on their pilgrimage, although a curious individual could seek them out for study. The divergent ones would only interfere at the behest of another organization. The hunters would observe them, but I don't think they could try anything. The same goes for the Uratha. Finally, the Sin-Eaters have no reason to get involved, unleast I can think in one.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding the Technocrats' stance on these new, not so new creatures.<br /> <br /> As for the Kindred, they would have a business relationship as I said before, but in general they will take an attitude similar to that of their original universe, that of non-intervention until necessary;<br /> <br /> I would say that the werewolves would not change much, they will of course gather information on how to fight them, but keeping their distance;<br /> <br /> I believe that the mages would try to maintain an armed peace while exchanging information on how magic works in this world and on the different factions that exist, only later deciding to ally or intervene;<br /> <br /> The beasts would be an interesting species, since there is nothing similar to them in their original world, so they could choose to interact with them for research purposes and perhaps cooperation, after all, beasts are useful adaptable;<br /> <br /> Arisen are a case study for them, after all, a creature that does not die can be very useful and the Arisen are usually very powerful, so they would try to capture one;<br /> <br /> The Lost and the Sin-eaters, I believe they would study the subject, but in general, just ignore them, because they have nothing that interests them at first sight, unless one develops an interest in souls, but a mage would be more viable;<br /> <br /> The demons... I think they would see them as objects of study and they would approach them believing that this would be a plan of the God-Machine, they would also be interested in the cryptids as guinea pigs;<br /> <br /> In the case of the Prometheans and the Divergents, they would have a very practical interest in them, because it is a way for them to accumulate more power within their faction, it might not work, but they would at least try and in the case of the Divergents, I believe it would work, in a way.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T09:38:20-07:00","id":1541589,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Technocrats would ignore anyone at all. It's their thing too to study RDs, as it is to study reality. They'd have an invested interest in understanding everyone and how they relate to the world at large, specially when that is necessary to understand this new reality.<br /> <br /> All splats have very relevant information and relationships to key aspects of how this world works.<br /> <br /> They would certainly become one of the Conspiracies that create Deviants, that's for sure, if they get enough time. And it is possible that their main antagonism would be with the other technological entity trying to control the entire world: the God-Machine. Although it doesn't necessarily means they'll work with Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T15:43:16-07:00","id":1541614,"title":"","content":"They wouldn't ignore them completely, I just think they wouldn't prioritize them because they would already have too much on their plate, so they would have to choose what to focus on until they gain stability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T18:45:43-07:00","id":1541622,"title":"","content":"Yes, but how to properly prioritize when you know nothing?<br /> <br /> Remember, in this setup they're completely in the dark about how this world works. They don't think about those splats as &quot;vampires, fairies, werewolves, etc&quot; in the same sense a native would, or a player, or even how they would think of RDs in their own reality. Instead, they're all &quot;natives&quot;.<br /> <br /> So they don't have a parameter to say which is a priority and which is not. And the many distinctions between those entities and their apparent counterparts in WoD would just reinforce that such judgements aren't safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T02:16:50-07:00","id":1541637,"title":"","content":"It's actually quite simple to prioritize if you take into account what I said earlier: some will interact with you and others will just observe and take care of their business. So you deal with the first group and keep the second group under observation. This is far from ideal, but the situation in question is also far from ideal in many ways. After all, I have a fraction of my power and money and no influence. I have to know how to use the resources I still have and get more, quickly, otherwise everything will collapse. If it sounds desperate, it's because it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T08:01:35-07:00","id":1541650,"title":"","content":"Not to be annoying, but has anyone ever thought about what the distribution of creatures would be like in this city in question? I mean, assuming that 1 in every 1000 was a creature of darkness (Yes, I took that number out) and assuming that they didn't go to a place where they are scarce, since there are beings of each main type then it must be a big city, I imagine. If it were New York for example, then there would be more than 8000 of them installed in the city, not counting the ones that arrived with the technocracy, the ones that must not be registered, in addition to non-human creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T12:53:03-07:00","id":1541659,"title":"","content":"To be honest, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28270\" data-vbnamecard=\"28270\">Yumlum</a> didn't even said they arrived in a city. As far as we know, they may very well be in a forgotten farm in Congo, in a dark recess of the Colombian Amazon jungle, or at the middle of the Pacific ocean between three or four Polynesian countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T17:06:02-07:00","id":1541665,"title":"","content":"Fair argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T20:36:17-07:00","id":1541674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541622#post1541622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but how to properly prioritize when you know nothing?<br /> <br /> Remember, in this setup they're completely in the dark about how this world works. They don't think about those splats as &quot;vampires, fairies, werewolves, etc&quot; in the same sense a native would, or a player, or even how they would think of RDs in their own reality. Instead, they're all &quot;natives&quot;.<br /> <br /> So they don't have a parameter to say which is a priority and which is not. And the many distinctions between those entities and their apparent counterparts in WoD would just reinforce that such judgements aren't safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Not only that, the Technocrats probably would even mistakenly confuse this new &quot;universe&quot; with some weird Deep Umbra realm or some weird Paradox Realm. As soon as they understand that Kansas has gone bye bye (which would be really quick), they would stop making assumptions about their surrounding reality.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, that may even lead them to NOT prioritize &quot;the mission&quot; - or even to totally discard it. That would greatly depend on what they assume that this reality is. Are these &quot;humans&quot; or &quot;sleepers&quot; around them really &quot;humans&quot;? If they try to detect the Avatars of said humans and don't find any, would they still consider these to be &quot;the masses&quot; that need protection? Or are all the billions of inhabitants of this reality a threat to the &quot;Frontlines&quot; (their &quot;base Earth&quot;) and therefore prone to extermination?<br /> <br /> The answers to these questions may pose them as &quot;folks' heroes&quot; or harbingers of doom.<br /> <br /> Since there's a possibility that they see everything in this reality as &quot;ultraterrestrials&quot; (just like extraterrestrials, but instead of being beings from other planets, it's beings from other dimensions), they may have no problem working with any kinds of local &quot;Reality Deviants&quot;, both towards making alliances and also brainwashing them.<br /> <br /> And in such case, their main priority besides growing in power in order to survive, would probably be &quot;research a way to go back home&quot;, rather than trying to &quot;protect the Masses&quot; (which they might not even recognize as being properly humans to begin with)<br /> <br /> And yes, I agree with Monteparnas that them and the God Machine would probably form the biggest antagonistic tensions in the setting.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I just remembered, how will their Spirit Sphere (Dimensional Science) work here? Will it give them access to the Supernal? Will it work on the native spirits? Does it also works on the spirits of the dead? (Ghosts). Remember, they don't have a &quot;Death Sphere&quot;, and their &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; should at least in theory work for anything that is not in the Material Plane.<br /> <br /> How exactly will that work thou? That's one crucial point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T02:55:10-07:00","id":1541681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541674#post1541674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Not only that, the Technocrats probably would even mistakenly confuse this new &quot;universe&quot; with some weird Deep Umbra realm or some weird Paradox Realm. As soon as they understand that Kansas has gone bye bye (which would be really quick), they would stop making assumptions about their surrounding reality.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, that may even lead them to NOT prioritize &quot;the mission&quot; - or even to totally discard it. That would greatly depend on what they assume that this reality is. Are these &quot;humans&quot; or &quot;sleepers&quot; around them really &quot;humans&quot;? If they try to detect the Avatars of said humans and don't find any, would they still consider these to be &quot;the masses&quot; that need protection? Or are all the billions of inhabitants of this reality a threat to the &quot;Frontlines&quot; (their &quot;base Earth&quot;) and therefore prone to extermination?<br /> <br /> The answers to these questions may pose them as &quot;folks' heroes&quot; or harbingers of doom.<br /> <br /> Since there's a possibility that they see everything in this reality as &quot;ultraterrestrials&quot; (just like extraterrestrials, but instead of being beings from other planets, it's beings from other dimensions), they may have no problem working with any kinds of local &quot;Reality Deviants&quot;, both towards making alliances and also brainwashing them.<br /> <br /> And in such case, their main priority besides growing in power in order to survive, would probably be &quot;research a way to go back home&quot;, rather than trying to &quot;protect the Masses&quot; (which they might not even recognize as being properly humans to begin with)<br /> <br /> And yes, I agree with Monteparnas that them and the God Machine would probably form the biggest antagonistic tensions in the setting.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I just remembered, how will their Spirit Sphere (Dimensional Science) work here? Will it give them access to the Supernal? Will it work on the native spirits? Does it also works on the spirits of the dead? (Ghosts). Remember, they don't have a &quot;Death Sphere&quot;, and their &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; should at least in theory work for anything that is not in the Material Plane.<br /> <br /> How exactly will that work thou? That's one crucial point</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul in CofD doesn't have the divine shard within them, doesn't change with Consensus, or be created even with Supernal Magic (Maybe the Archmage can but I don't remember) so I don't think Technocracy will recognize them as the human from their reality, but still human enough that only the most heartless Technocrat could kill in such cold blooded manner. <br /> <br /> I think Spirit Sphere work on local spirit, but it would need some adjusting, I think they can't go to the Supernal realm, because they're only limited to Sphere 5 of everything and so their Arete cap at 5. But they can go to the Hedge, surface of the Underworld, Shadow, Empyrean and other realm that are like them, but not Duat, Arcadia, Primodial Dream, whereever the Divine Fire, the lower depth of Underworld come from and other such realm. To interact with CofD ghost they would need Entropy and Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T08:13:22-07:00","id":1541685,"title":"","content":"I don't think they'll turn to genocide, as there's no actual reason to think those people will invade the Front Lines.<br /> <br /> But Technocrats can get pretty heartless for the mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T15:43:40-07:00","id":1541708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541681#post1541681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soul in CofD doesn't have the divine shard within them, doesn't change with Consensus, or be created even with Supernal Magic (Maybe the Archmage can but I don't remember) so I don't think Technocracy will recognize them as the human from their reality, but still human enough that only the most heartless Technocrat could kill in such cold blooded manner.<br /> <br /> I think Spirit Sphere work on local spirit, but it would need some adjusting, I think they can't go to the Supernal realm, because they're only limited to Sphere 5 of everything and so their Arete cap at 5. But they can go to the Hedge, surface of the Underworld, Shadow, Empyrean and other realm that are like them, but not Duat, Arcadia, Primodial Dream, whereever the Divine Fire, the lower depth of Underworld come from and other such realm. To interact with CofD ghost they would need Entropy and Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arete 5 allows them to reach Dimensional Science 5 (Spirit 5), which is enough to transpose the Horizon and reach the Deep Umbra, which is the place for all the Eldritch and unknownable stuff. I'd say that, if they can adjust their Dimensional Science to this new reality, then they could reach anywhere in it.<br /> <br /> Technocrats can create &quot;souls&quot; and/or Avatars (if they are distinct things). That requires Dimensional Science / Spirit 5, but it is manageable.<br /> <br /> They can also create or &quot;manipulate&quot; spirits - aka they can turn a Spirit into something else, or create tailored spirit kinds.<br /> <br /> All of those capabilities will need to be addressed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T07:30:40-07:00","id":1541736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541685#post1541685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they'll turn to genocide, as there's no actual reason to think those people will invade the Front Lines.<br /> <br /> But Technocrats can get pretty heartless for the mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably more likely; they wouldn't be able to enact genocide on an entire existence anyway, even if they wanted to.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree, they wouldn't want to.<br /> <br /> But &quot;The Mission&quot; would NOT be to protect those &quot;simulacrums&quot; of humans, as they would see them, which means that they would be free from that burden, therefore their most important objectives would be first to survive, obviously, second to grow in power - in order to survive and to accomplish their other objectives, not merely for power's sake, third to study and acquire knowledge of this new reality - again, for the sake of the 2 previous goals, and finally at forth, finding a way to go back - which might as well be absolutely impossible, but they wouldn't know that and would try nevertheless.<br /> <br /> Considering the &quot;humans&quot; of the setting as &quot;simulacrums&quot; also opens them up to be much more open to deal with other &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; of the setting - since in their minds, EVERYBODY there will be RDs. Therefore, dealing with &quot;sleepers&quot; is no less troublesome than dealing with the &quot;vampiric simulacrums&quot; or any other splats. It would be no different from dealing with the many denizens of an Umbral world that they could be lost into - and in fact, they would probably think that they are lost within some weird Realm within the Deep Umbra (and they might even be right). This, anything goes - alliances with these critters, recruiting them, whatever it takes, it's all valid, but they are all just &quot;disposable assets&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T21:43:24-07:00","id":1542502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1541674#post1541674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I just remembered, how will their Spirit Sphere (Dimensional Science) work here? Will it give them access to the Supernal? Will it work on the native spirits? Does it also works on the spirits of the dead? (Ghosts). Remember, they don't have a &quot;Death Sphere&quot;, and their &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; should at least in theory work for anything that is not in the Material Plane.<br /> <br /> How exactly will that work thou? That's one crucial point</div> </div> </div> </div>Coming in late, but:<br /> <br /> How will <i>any</i> of their Spheres work? They're in a universe with completely different metaphysics, where actual reality-warping Magick isn't a thing outside of the mythical acts of Imperium performed by Archmasters. It's entirely possible that their Spheres and Hedge Paths <i>don't work </i>in the Chronicles of Darkness. And if they <i>do </i>work, they don't necessarily work the same way.<br /> <br /> Break out the <b>Mage Translation Guide</b>, everyone; we're gonna need it here. Granted, it's somewhat out of date, because it was translating between <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> Revised Edition and <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> first edition; and both gamelines have moved on to new editions since then. But it's still mostly relevant.<br /> <br /> My gut instinct would be to define two kinds of mages for this: the Supernal Mages are the ones native to the Chronicles of Darkness, Awakened by the Watchtowers to manipulate the Supernal symbols in the Fallen World; and the Phenomenal Mages who hail from the World of Darkness. Phenomenal Mages don't Awaken to Watchtowers, and aren't split up into Paths; instead, each Phenomenal Mage is uniquely Awakened by a resident deep within her Oneiros formally known as her Genius. Her Magick isn't performed by manipulating Supernal symbols, but by <i>directly</i> shaping the Phenomenal World.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats would be Phenomenal Mages, and conceptually would use Spheres instead of Arcana. This would include Entropy instead of Death and Fate, and a Spirit Sphere that's capable of reaching any of the Otherworlds in the cosmology rather than being limited to the Shadow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T22:03:37-07:00","id":1542503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1542502#post1542502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How will <i>any</i> of their Spheres work? They're in a universe with completely different metaphysics, where actual reality-warping Magick isn't a thing outside of the mythical acts of Imperium performed by Archmasters. It's entirely possible that their Spheres and Hedge Paths <i>don't work </i>in the Chronicles of Darkness. And if they <i>do </i>work, they don't necessarily work the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked those same questions in another version of this thread, but Yumlum wants this exercise to run with their magic working as always because reasons, even if here and there they try to come up with limitations that don\u2019t really pertain to them.<br /> <br /> My personal take? Technocrats within the CoD would lose access to their magic, except maybe within their Oneiros. From there, they may develop a new set of powers based on their Avatars, maybe Hedge Magic, maybe they Awaken to new and strange Watchtowers, maybe they get to be something even stranger.<br /> <br /> But their native powers? That\u2019s a lot of bullshit for this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T08:26:12-07:00","id":1542527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1542503#post1542503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked those same questions in another version of this thread, but Yumlum wants this exercise to run with their magic working as always <u>because reasons</u>, even if here and there they try to come up with limitations that don\u2019t really pertain to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The underlined part is the only part I take issue with. If you <i>define </i>the reasons, that's fine. Thus my talk about Supernal and Phenomenal Mages.<br /> <br /> The ironic thing is that if you do this, then Phenomenal Mages are the guys in the Chronicles of Darkness who are directly warping reality, as opposed to the Supernals who are imposing a Higher Truth onto the Lie. Which means that the Technocrats, who in their own setting are nominally the champions of objective truth, in this scenario are the only ones who are utilizing subjective reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1542503#post1542503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take? Technocrats within the CoD would lose access to their magic, except maybe within their Oneiros. From there, they may develop a new set of powers based on their Avatars, maybe Hedge Magic, maybe they Awaken to new and strange Watchtowers, maybe they get to be something even stranger.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the likes of the God Machine on the one hand, and Hunter Conspiracies and Deviant's Web of Pain on the other, the boundaries of &quot;science&quot; in the Chronicles of Darkness are a lot fuzzier than they are in the World of Darkness. If the Technocrats <i>were </i>to lose their Enlightenment and Spheres upon arrival in the Chronicles of Darkness, I have no doubt that they'd rebuild themselves as a combination of these factors.<br /> <br /> Heck, even if they <i>retain</i> their reality-warping Magick, I could see Iteration X learning of the God-Machine and thinking of it as this world's manifestation of Autochthonia (which, too be fair, it might actually be); I could see the Progenitors infiltrating the Cheiron Group and/or becoming a Conspiracy in the Web of Pain. The New World Order might found a Hunter Conspiracy with an Endowment that's a combination of spy-tech and social engineering; or they might end up joining the Cryptocracy from <b>Contagion Chronicle</b>. The <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> makes a brief mention of a group known as the Gnomes of Zurich; I'm pretty sure the Syndicate would find some common ground with them. Frankly, the Void Engineers would likely be the ones who get hit the hardest by the change, as the Chronicles of Darkness don't have anything akin to the Etherspace or Deep Universe that they seek to tame or fight. They don't really have much of anything to do off-world; so they're largely refocused on their on-planet divisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1542503#post1542503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But their native powers? That\u2019s a lot of bullshit for this setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>A space can be made for it, though. That's something that the Chronicles of Darkness excels at: making space for additional weirdness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Expanded on the final point. 09-23-2024, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T13:49:25-07:00","id":1542578,"title":"","content":"I agree with almost everything you said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>.<br /> <br /> As far as science goes though, the Technocracy is far more than just the Conspiracy of Science, although it\u2019s also that. I think that something coming from their Avatars, even if not necessarily Enlightenment as they previously understood it, isn\u2019t just likely, but more interesting (which is more important).<br /> <br /> My take is that while they may end up being a small organization on reach due to their lack of manpower, they\u2019ll probably surpass most or even all native organizations on sheer scope. They\u2019ll run the whole gamut of Weird Science as they pick up things, on top of whatever thing they become themselves.<br /> <br /> But the one thing I actually disagree with, albeit minor, is that the Void Engineers would be at some disadvantage. Sure, a good portion of their space faring infrastructure would be useless or next to it. But assuming a multi-Convention Construct (as it seems to be the case for this exercise), the VEs present are unlikely to be space-farers to begin with (unless it is a space construct, which would be very interesting on its own), and in the CoD they have plenty of strange places to investigate that they don\u2019t need to believe to exist before they can explore.<br /> <br /> Just imagine VEs establishing outposts in the Underworld, the Shadow, the Hedge, all that before we even consider access to some special power to reach places. And if someone can finally reach the Supernal, it surely is the Void Engineers. And they can also find ways to implement that space-traveling infrastructure within other realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T15:19:54-07:00","id":1542649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1542578#post1542578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with almost everything you said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>.<br /> <br /> As far as science goes though, the Technocracy is far more than just the Conspiracy of Science, although it\u2019s also that. I think that something coming from their Avatars, even if not necessarily Enlightenment as they previously understood it, isn\u2019t just likely, but more interesting (which is more important).<br /> <br /> My take is that while they may end up being a small organization on reach due to their lack of manpower, they\u2019ll probably surpass most or even all native organizations on sheer scope. They\u2019ll run the whole gamut of Weird Science as they pick up things, on top of whatever thing they become themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of the most interesting approach to use for them, I'd probably go with a combination of the Phenomenal Mages thing I was talking about before (that is, apply enough translations from Ascension to Awakened to let you do a convincing facsimile of the former using the latter) with the Gifted Science chapter from the <b>Awakening StoryteStoryteller's Guide</b>. <i>And</i> have them infiltrate the various Science-oriented groups in the Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T17:25:05-07:00","id":1543466,"title":"","content":"I imagine they would view it as a better version than theirs. Threats like the Antideluvians don't seem to exist. Nephandi don't either. Less of a situation of worrying of the world ending and more just mundanity supernatural existence. I don't think they would abandon their own earth but they would likely use Chronicles as a recruitment ground. Given the Union is so underground in WoD that basically no other splats have an inkling they exist outside of those involved with them, on the payroll or a few Tremere I don't even think the union would appear on most of the Chronicle's splat's radar. The only groups I could see even noticing the union would be the mages and VASCU. Vascu due to them being actual feds and psychic, so they could get poached or stumble across them. And the other Mages because they would likely realize a good portion of freshly awakened are getting poached and its not by the seers or left handed paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-31T18:04:15-08:00","id":1557167,"title":"","content":"Not meaning to necro, but this thread has been fascinating in general, and I'd like to add my two cents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1543466#post1543466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine they would view it as a better version than theirs. Threats like the Antideluvians don't seem to exist. Nephandi don't either. Less of a situation of worrying of the world ending and more just mundanity supernatural existence. I don't think they would abandon their own earth but they would likely use Chronicles as a recruitment ground. Given the Union is so underground in WoD that basically no other splats have an inkling they exist outside of those involved with them, on the payroll or a few Tremere I don't even think the union would appear on most of the Chronicle's splat's radar. The only groups I could see even noticing the union would be the mages and VASCU. Vascu due to them being actual feds and psychic, so they could get poached or stumble across them. And the other Mages because they would likely realize a good portion of freshly awakened are getting poached and its not by the seers or left handed paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue the opposite. They traded a dozen blood gods they could kill, and in their place they got the Exarchs, tyrant gods, and a mess of other enemies. They got the God-Machine, the True Fae, the gods that might exist in the underworld, the abyss and the scelesti is a thing they now have to fight, every archmage is a literal god of reality. The Tremere are also still around, but now as a major order of liches who eat souls.<br /> <br /> And that's the obvious enemies. Luna is a lunatic screaming into the void and is a prison of alien void gods and the firstborn aren't pushovers either. The judges and arisen are rather ooc for the technocracy, especially with them being non-linearly bound to time. The demons all work to blow up infrastructure and technocrats stuff has enough of a resemblance. <br /> <br /> The Pentacle likely is going to think the technocracy is Seer aligned at first, the Free Council especially, given the Seers' attempt to make their own technocracy before the Great Refusal. The Guardians likely are going to be the first to notice them, because the Labyrinth makes a number of awakened and they'd notice if their prodigies are vanishing suddenly. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T00:04:57-08:00","id":1557170,"title":"","content":"There are definite parallels between the Seers of the Throne and the Technocracy. Setting aside the technology issue, the Panopticon closely parallels the NWO's surveillance state objective, and the Hegemony closely parallels the NWO's attempts at social engineering through political entities; and the Ministry of Mammon is very much akin to the Syndicate. And I wouldn't be surprised to see the NWO and the Syndicate attempting to infiltrate and possibly incorporate their Seer counterparts. <br /> <br /> The main difference between the two is that the Seers of the Throne are more purely a study of seeking power for the sake of power; the Technocracy was designed to represent a more subtle trap that intellects tend to be particularly vulnerable to: the tendency to fall in love with your theories and to want to bend reality to match your models when the two disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T18:27:33-08:00","id":1557197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557170#post1557170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference between the two is that the Seers of the Throne are more purely a study of seeking power for the sake of power; the Technocracy was designed to represent a more subtle trap that intellects tend to be particularly vulnerable to: the tendency to fall in love with your theories and to want to bend reality to match your models when the two disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some limited ways, the difference between the Seers and the Technocoracy is the difference between Fascism and Communism. With the Seers as the former and the Technocoracy as the latter. The Technocoracy profoundly sees themselves as the good guys and in many ways they are virtuous. Their virtues make them deadly and richly compelling villains. You see both their nobility and why they must be stopped. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T09:03:48-08:00","id":1557208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557197#post1557197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In some limited ways, the difference between the Seers and the Technocoracy is the difference between Fascism and Communism. With the Seers as the former and the Technocoracy as the latter. The Technocoracy profoundly sees themselves as the good guys and in many ways they are virtuous. Their virtues make them deadly and richly compelling villains. You see both their nobility and why they must be stopped.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right. The seers know they are quislings and serving tyrant gods, none of them think they are heroes or if they do, they are deeply delusional. The technocracy, for all its many flaws, believes it is doing good for mankind.<br /> <br /> First contact might have diplomatic contact, but the technocracy as a whole isn't going to want to work with a group that wants humanity to forever be under the boot of tyrants. Syndicate might but not the other paradigms. Though they probably will have some defectors.<br /> <br /> IMO if they don't start killing each other first, the technocracy and the free council might get along very well or at least better than with other reality deviants. <br /> <br /> Also thinking about it, the void engineers would salivate at the hedge having paths in space and a changeling freehold on the moon. (Though depending on their approach with changelings, I could see it being like TSV ala &quot;These guys are victims and need support and we can provide it in exchange for allies&quot; in the sense that changelings are practically poster boys for the dangers of reality deviants and what the Union protects the world against.)<br /> <br /> Some other thoughts,<br /> <br /> Someone in the Union is going to assume someone is fucking with them when they hear that somehow the Tremere are also present. Same as if they find the Aeon of the Abyss and are confused as to how Voormas is also present if they know who that is.<br /> <br /> Hunter Conspiracies like TFV, I could see getting poached or taken over by the Union as shock troops or as a way to get field agents quickly after the depleted Union's arrival. <br /> <br /> Sin-eaters might be confused at first for mages/RD's from wod with their geists confused for avatars though that would be corrected pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T16:43:48-08:00","id":1557214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557208#post1557208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. The seers know they are quislings and serving tyrant gods, none of them think they are heroes or if they do, they are deeply delusional. The technocracy, for all its many flaws, believes it is doing good for mankind.<br /> <br /> First contact might have diplomatic contact, but the technocracy as a whole isn't going to want to work with a group that wants humanity to forever be under the boot of tyrants. Syndicate might but not the other paradigms. Though they probably will have some defectors.<br /> <br /> IMO if they don't start killing each other first, the technocracy and the free council might get along very well or at least better than with other reality deviants.<br /> <br /> Also thinking about it, the void engineers would salivate at the hedge having paths in space and a changeling freehold on the moon. (Though depending on their approach with changelings, I could see it being like TSV ala &quot;These guys are victims and need support and we can provide it in exchange for allies&quot; in the sense that changelings are practically poster boys for the dangers of reality deviants and what the Union protects the world against.)<br /> <br /> Some other thoughts,<br /> <br /> Someone in the Union is going to assume someone is fucking with them when they hear that somehow the Tremere are also present. Same as if they find the Aeon of the Abyss and are confused as to how Voormas is also present if they know who that is.<br /> <br /> Hunter Conspiracies like TFV, I could see getting poached or taken over by the Union as shock troops or as a way to get field agents quickly after the depleted Union's arrival.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters might be confused at first for mages/RD's from wod with their geists confused for avatars though that would be corrected pretty quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of the Technocoracy building alliances works. You could do a campaign themed on a struggle for redemption. C:L changelings are built on a metaphor of victims striving to become survivors. Mages are striving towards a fulfillment of a different kind. Changelings, Free Council and the Technocoracy, healing and growing together. It might sound cheesy but it's actually deep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T05:44:17-08:00","id":1557229,"title":"","content":"I think the Technocracy would definitely oppose the Seers of the Throne. The Seers are a corruption of everything the Technocracy stands for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 01-03-2026, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T07:41:57-08:00","id":1557230,"title":"","content":"Of course, so is the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Seers=fascists, Technocrats=communists&quot; comparison is imperfect (in particular, the Syndicate represents the Capitalism that the workers will rise up against in Communist theory); but it's surprisingly informative of the essential natures of the two: substitute &quot;the Exarchs&quot; for the State, and fascism is a perfect match for the Seers. (And since the Hierarchy is fundamentally about the State, it's an exact match for them.) <br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy, the parallel is that both Technocrats (&quot;rule by experts&quot;) and Communists are operating on theories about how to being about a Utopian future; and both encounter the problem that Utopias don't work in the real world and inevitably lead those who are truly invested in bringing them about to compromise their ideals in an effort to force it to work. The Technocracy differs from Communism in terms of what their end goals are; in the same way that fascism is properly specific to the Hierarchy while other Ministries have fascism-adjacent ideologies (e.g., Paternoster is all about how organized religion can be used as a means to enslave), the NWO's end-game comes closest to Communism, while the other Conventions have their own ideas of what Mass Ascension should look like. <br /> <br /> Another parallel to the Fascism vs. Communism comparison is that there's a sort of horseshoe-like effect where they're so polarized opposite that they sort of bend back around and start to resemble each other. So too with the Technocracy and the Seers: the former seek to empower humanity while the latter seek to enslave humanity; but the Utopian ideals of the Technocracy have caused it to &quot;bend around&quot; to the point of pushing for totalitarian solutions to the fact that reality simply isn't operating the way they think it should. So Seer and Technocrat both find themselves attempting to control people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T08:45:38-08:00","id":1557232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557230#post1557230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, so is the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So Seer and Technocrat both find themselves attempting to control people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree but they do it in such different ways, and the technocracy at least believes it is working toward a common good, that the two groups will be incompatible and quickly hate one another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the Technocracy would definitely oppose the Seers of the Throne. The Seers are a corruption of everything the Technocracy stands for.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Agreed Amethyst, if absolutely nothing else, the Exarchs are something the Union won't accept because their very nature is that of tyrant gods who want to keep the masses miserable and suffering and enslaved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T11:38:39-08:00","id":1557236,"title":"","content":"The ironic thing is that the Technocracy has Control, which may very well be tyrant gods; the Union just doesn't know it. <br /> <br /> That said, a Technocracy stranded in the Chronicles of Darkness probably <i>doesn't </i>have Control; that would make them more like the Technocracy of the Convention Books, where they were cut off from Control and developed now grounded command structures for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T01:41:27-08:00","id":1557334,"title":"","content":"The first thing I want to call out is that Communism and &quot;the American view of Communism through cherry-picked and shallowly explained examples&quot; are very distinct things. And fascist-like authoritarian regimes are far from something relegated only to communism and actual fascism. Liberal authoritarian states like Bukele's El Salvador are far from a rare thing. This isn't just a myopic view of communist ideologies (which are many), it's also a dangerously myopic view of authoritarianism and how it happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557170#post1557170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are definite parallels between the Seers of the Throne and the Technocracy. Setting aside the technology issue, the Panopticon closely parallels the NWO's surveillance state objective, and the Hegemony closely parallels the NWO's attempts at social engineering through political entities; and the Ministry of Mammon is very much akin to the Syndicate. And I wouldn't be surprised to see the NWO and the Syndicate attempting to infiltrate and possibly incorporate their Seer counterparts.<br /> <br /> The main difference between the two is that the Seers of the Throne are more purely a study of seeking power for the sake of power; the Technocracy was designed to represent a more subtle trap that intellects tend to be particularly vulnerable to: the tendency to fall in love with your theories and to want to bend reality to match your models when the two disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The similarity isn't surprising when we remember that 1st edition Technocracy was basically every conspiracy theory about secret world domination given form, and only later would it get nuanced explanations. The Union is meant to be a case study of a system corrupting its core goals to perpetuate itself.<br /> <br /> Yet, precisely because of this, small differences in thought go a long way, so I don't think the Union would want to be buddies with the Seers <i>in principle</i>.<br /> <br /> But what I think is kind of lost in this debate is that <i>this Union is stranded in another world</i>. Are the humans here even real humans for them? Is this Earth just as valid and worth of their work as the Earth they came from? How does this place even works, what's out there? Those are not simple questions that we really can assume any actual group would default to a given answer.<br /> <br /> Void Engineers in particular would have a field day, but not because of Hedge, Space or whatever. Instead, it's because the very world they're in is alien and strange, ripe for exploration. They don't know which laws of nature or supernature work here (and they're not the same), they don't know what's happening behind the scenes, they don't even know the basics of human psychology for the people from this world. And news flash: <i><b>there are relevant species-wide differences</b></i>.<br /> <br /> For every other Convention things are very different. It isn't just that they'll have to decide what to do about each supernatural society, is that they're cut from the very institutions that define them, and have defined them for a long time. As those institutions have been put in place by their oldest predecessors and evolved along the <i>thing</i> that would become the Union, the modern Conventions never before even <i><b>existed</b></i> without such structure.<br /> <br /> What's the Syndicate without knowledge or access to any company at all? What's the NWO when its whole membership is half a dozen guys (if that much) stranded in an unknown city where they don't know anyone, there are no insiders in any institution and they don't even know current politics? What's the Progenitors and Iteration X without labs, financing, contacts in academia and related companies? The fun of such a game would be exactly the fact that those Agents are completely Lost in Space.<br /> <br /> Not to say, as I already explored before, that we don't really know if their Magic will even work here in the same way, or any way at all. All similarities aside, CoD and WoD are based on radically different metaphysics, and the very concepts that power each Mage splat simply do not exist in the other setting. Reality in CoD is mysterious and unknown, but set. There's no fluctuating Tellurian that let someone alter it just with willpower, even if there are forces that react to willpower to do something. WoD has no Supernal Realms housing the true laws of reality. They are metaphysically incompatible, they are <b>not</b> the same splat, and even if their powers work the same way, it will be for unknown reasons that may become themselves a matter for investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T14:50:12-08:00","id":1557383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness#post1540876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's assume a building full of Technocrat (25 Mage, 100 Extraordinary Citizen, 500 Sleeper) suddenly find themselves in the Chronicle of Darkness, within a city where every Splat exist. How would the Technocrat react to the various supernatural creature of this new night? Technocrat power are also very diminish, with Arete 5 being the most they could have, and Extraordinary Citizen can only have Max 3 dot in any path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocrats wouldn't just be diminished, they'd practically cease to exist, due to how both universes handle the existence of magic. As far as I'm aware, there's no Tower of Technomancy to be found in Awakening.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say they would join on with the Seers of the Throne, as those are probably the closest thing they have to upholding their desired paradigm. But even that would be a bitter pill to swallow, as the world is still under the thumb of godly powerful wizards who control reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T13:19:36-08:00","id":1557712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557334#post1557334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to say, as I already explored before, that we don't really know if their Magic will even work here in the same way, or any way at all. All similarities aside, CoD and WoD are based on radically different metaphysics, and the very concepts that power each Mage splat simply do not exist in the other setting. Reality in CoD is mysterious and unknown, but set. There's no fluctuating Tellurian that let someone alter it just with willpower, even if there are forces that react to willpower to do something. WoD has no Supernal Realms housing the true laws of reality. They are metaphysically incompatible, they are <b>not</b> the same splat, and even if their powers work the same way, it will be for unknown reasons that may become themselves a matter for investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, I will point out there is no <i>Tower of Technomancy</i> that I am familiar with in Awakening.<br /> <br /> Your magic comes from the world of Demons, Angels, Faeries, Spirits or Wraiths. If the Technocracy want to keep practicing their super science, they're going to have to accept the existence of magic, and adapt their technology to comply with it.<br /> <br /> Which, as I type this, I am now imagining a <b>Mastigos Technocrat</b> building '<i>The Unmaker'</i> from <b>Doom</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T14:53:38-08:00","id":1557713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557383#post1557383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technocrats wouldn't just be diminished, they'd practically cease to exist, due to how both universes handle the existence of magic. As far as I'm aware, there's no Tower of Technomancy to be found in Awakening.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say they would join on with the Seers of the Throne, as those are probably the closest thing they have to upholding their desired paradigm. But even that would be a bitter pill to swallow, as the world is still under the thumb of godly powerful wizards who control reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557712#post1557712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again, I will point out there is no <i>Tower of Technomancy</i> that I am familiar with in Awakening.<br /> <br /> Your magic comes from the world of Demons, Angels, Faeries, Spirits or Wraiths. If the Technocracy want to keep practicing their super science, they're going to have to accept the existence of magic, and adapt their technology to comply with it.<br /> <br /> Which, as I type this, I am now imagining a <b>Mastigos Technocrat</b> building '<i>The Unmaker'</i> from <b>Doom</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>...why would they need to do any of that? An Ascension Mage's magic comes from themselves. They don't need Towers to function. It's not like traveling to other universes is somehow going to turn it off. Especially when Void Engineers do travel to other universes with foreign Umbras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T15:36:15-08:00","id":1557715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557713#post1557713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...why would they need to do any of that? An Ascension Mage's magic comes from themselves. They don't need Towers to function. It's not like traveling to other universes is somehow going to turn it off. Especially when Void Engineers do travel to other universes with foreign Umbras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the Technocoracy could help the local Mages find better sources of power. If no one needed what the Exarchs monopolize, if the abyss held no power over magic, mages could build utopia in this reality. Remember, Utopia is technically possible in this reality, it's blocked by the Seers and the Exarchs. If the Technocrats could link these mages with their own magic then the Exarchs, the Seers and two points of the Atlantian diamond become irrelevant. More importantly, the Technocrats can liberate themselves and become real heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-17-2026, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T15:41:05-08:00","id":1557716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557713#post1557713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...why would they need to do any of that? An Ascension Mage's magic comes from themselves. They don't need Towers to function. It's not like traveling to other universes is somehow going to turn it off. Especially when Void Engineers do travel to other universes with foreign Umbras.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my assumption that by transferring to the other universe, they would also be subjected to its rules. As others have pointed out, the mechanical functions of magic are fundamentally different in Awakening from how they work in Ascension.<br /> <br /> Awakening does not have a tellurian, or an Umbra, or a free style approach to magic. It has the Supernal Realms, Watchtowers and Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T01:23:48-08:00","id":1557721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557715#post1557715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps the Technocoracy could help the local Mages find better sources of power. If no one needed what the Exarchs monopolize, if the abyss held no power over magic, mages could build utopia in this reality. Remember, Utopia is technically possible in this reality, it's blocked by the Seers and the Exarchs. If the Technocrats could link these mages with their own magic then the Exarchs, the Seers and two points of the Atlantian diamond become irrelevant. More importantly, the Technocrats can liberate themselves and become real heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That honestly depends on the intent of the writer/ST. It is possible but also well, 25 Mages with no true way to increase their numbers isn't going to help their case. Now, if I was writing a story, I would have them be an Everett diplomatic/monitoring Construct rather than full-on stranding them in there. That way there would be some wiggle work and play on logistics, support lines and goals.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557716#post1557716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was my assumption that by transferring to the other universe, they would also be subjected to its rules. As others have pointed out, the mechanical functions of magic are fundamentally different in Awakening from how they work in Ascension.<br /> <br /> Awakening does not have a tellurian, or an Umbra, or a free style approach to magic. It has the Supernal Realms, Watchtowers and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if by that logic, they are subjected to its rules, Ascension Mages can break the rules of foreign realities and still do the stuff they can do normally.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ratings of Realms can be positive or negative. For example, a Realm that exists only in two-dimensional space (as in the book Flatland) might have a Correspondence rating of -4, reflecting that its reality is much more limited in terms of dimensional space than is Earth's. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that certain Realms have negative Sphere ratings. Actions and perceptions that are standard and normal on Earth are miraculous in such Realms and will require the use of static or dynamic magick. For example, to lift an object in a Realm with a Correspondence rating of -4, where the only &quot;true&quot; directions are forward/backward and right/left, the mage must perform magick.\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T04:06:31-08:00","id":1557722,"title":"","content":"It also has a design philosophy that there's always more out there than what the main gamelines depict. Even within the context of <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, you also have the Archmasters' Golden Roads, which operate outside of the five Paths and their Watchtowers; and there are indications that in the Time Before, mages were able to Awaken to the Supernal without the need for Watchtowers or Paths. <br /> <br /> But I wouldn't limit myself to Supernal Magic, operating on the premise of the manipulation of Supernal symbols to manipulate the Fallen (or Phenomenal) World. There's nothing saying that the Willworking Magick of <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> <i>doesn't</i> work in the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> setting; just that it's not how <i>Supernal Magic</i> works. Willworking uses different metaphysics, but not necessarily <i>incompatible </i>with the overall metaphysics of the CoD setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T06:42:29-08:00","id":1557725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557722#post1557722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also has a design philosophy that there's always more out there than what the main gamelines depict. Even within the context of <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, you also have the Archmasters' Golden Roads, which operate outside of the five Paths and their Watchtowers; and there are indications that in the Time Before, mages were able to Awaken to the Supernal without the need for Watchtowers or Paths.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't limit myself to Supernal Magic, operating on the premise of the manipulation of Supernal symbols to manipulate the Fallen (or Phenomenal) World. There's nothing saying that the Willworking Magick of <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> <i>doesn't</i> work in the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> setting; just that it's not how <i>Supernal Magic</i> works. Willworking uses different metaphysics, but not necessarily <i>incompatible </i>with the overall metaphysics of the CoD setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the trailer for the game, it seems that the Watchtowers were constructed for the purpose of teaching people how to access the Supernal, after the fall shut everybody off from them.<br /> <br /> Which now that I think about it, is a bit confusing. If the Exarchs don't want people to awaken to magic, and they are currently the rulers of the Supernal realms, why don't they simply destroy the towers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T09:18:47-08:00","id":1557729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557716#post1557716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was my assumption that by transferring to the other universe, they would also be subjected to its rules. As others have pointed out, the mechanical functions of magic are fundamentally different in Awakening from how they work in Ascension.<br /> <br /> Awakening does not have a tellurian, or an Umbra, or a free style approach to magic. It has the Supernal Realms, Watchtowers and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tellurian is a thing, and the shadow also exists<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going by the trailer for the game, it seems that the Watchtowers were constructed for the purpose of teaching people how to access the Supernal, after the fall shut everybody off from them. </div> </div> </div>We have trailers for awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T09:57:16-08:00","id":1557731,"title":"","content":"I'll bet you're picturing the Supernal as a land that's divided up into five Realms. That's not really accurate. A slightly more accurate picture (though still wildly inaccurate) would be of five islands in a vast ocean. The islands aren't what the Exarchs rule; they're the rebel fortresses that the Oracles created. Every time a mage becomes an archmaster, he does so by establishing a new island in that ocean, which is now his domain. <br /> <br /> The ocean is what the Exarchs rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T12:03:32-08:00","id":1557734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557725#post1557725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going by the trailer for the game, it seems that the Watchtowers were constructed for the purpose of teaching people how to access the Supernal, after the fall shut everybody off from them.<br /> <br /> Which now that I think about it, is a bit confusing. If the Exarchs don't want people to awaken to magic, and they are currently the rulers of the Supernal realms, why don't they simply destroy the towers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they simply can't. There may be other forces acting to keep humanity linked to the Supernal. Those forces might be friendly to humanity or simply find humans useful tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T12:06:28-08:00","id":1557735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557731#post1557731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll bet you're picturing the Supernal as a land that's divided up into five Realms. That's not really accurate. A slightly more accurate picture (though still wildly inaccurate) would be of five islands in a vast ocean. The islands aren't what the Exarchs rule; they're the rebel fortresses that the Oracles created. Every time a mage becomes an archmaster, he does so by establishing a new island in that ocean, which is now his domain.<br /> <br /> The ocean is what the Exarchs rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the creation of a new set of towers would be and epic campaign for Archmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T13:14:11-08:00","id":1557736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557729#post1557729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have trailers for awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E604uxkVqhk\" data-code=\"E604uxkVqhk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/E604uxkVqhk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T11:41:45-08:00","id":1557764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557735#post1557735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then the creation of a new set of towers would be and epic campaign for Archmages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would. In fact, it would likely involve a set of Ascensions, each establishing a new Watchtower in a new Oracle's former Cintimani. (A Cintimani is what an archmaster has instead of a Watchtower Realm: it is the Supernal terminus of his Golden Road.) <br /> <br /> Note that <i>all </i>quests for Ascension are epic campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T23:06:38-08:00","id":1558175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557712#post1557712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which, as I type this, I am now imagining a <b>Mastigos Technocrat</b> building '<i>The Unmaker'</i> from <b>Doom</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gun that feeds off the demonic energy of its victims and turns it back on them?<br /> <br /> Great, now I'm feeling inspired to come up with some ideas of my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T23:46:17-08:00","id":1558215,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with all of the assumptions that the Technocrats could take over the world are missing a major factor in the presented scenario. They have <i>25 mages.</i> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s it. 25 Mages, 100 Extra Ordinary Citizens, and 500 sleepers. That\u2019s not a small number, mind you, but in a completely different world, built on fundamentally different paradigms than they\u2019re used to? With no way to get any more back up or more requisitions from home? With none of the actual worldwide <i>structure</i> that the Technocracy has painstakingly built over the centuries that lets it be such an effective Conspiracy? Where their methods of control are already being used by many members of the Web of Pain, who most likely aren\u2019t interested in some mages trying to move in on their turf? In a world with thousands of this new mage type, Arisen and their cults, and the <i>God-Machine?</i> <br /> <br /> Hell, the Cheiron board would probably remind them of certain technocracy heads.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a lot they can do. But with 25 mages, they\u2019re not taking over the world. <br /> <br /> That being said, their experience in CofD has the potential to be <i>super</i> interesting. Cut off from their superiors, how will this small group evolve? What will they do when they realize that their methods of manipulating consensus mean nothing because there is no consensus? That the supernatural beings here aren\u2019t reality deviants, but built into the framework of the universe? Their whole framework for their mission, their reason for being the global conspiracy that they are, is defunct because reality literally doesn\u2019t <i>work</i> that way here. <br /> <br /> They still have their mission to protect humanity, especially if they\u2019re the idealistic type. And hell, without the mess of bureaucracy and asshole superiors, they might even feel freed up to do it even better. Research this new place, figure out who the true enemies of humanity are here. The local mages aren\u2019t making life for humanity worse via consensus. They might still dislike them on principle, but it\u2019s not like they\u2019ll be punished by superiors if they team up with ones like the Free Council. Like people have said, the Seers and their Exarchs are the sorts of mages the Technocrats would oppose on principle. The True Fae are obviously horrors that would fit right in with some of the existential monstrosities they deal with back home. And what\u2019s this about a God-Machine determined to keep everyone oppressed and miserable so that it can maintain its own status quo? (Who knows, this one might even trigger some self reflection about the ways in which the Technocracy has harmed the people it aimed to protect. Maybe.) <br /> <br /> Idk, I just think that beyond making this a \u201cmy mage is better than yours\u201d contest, there\u2019s a lot of cool potential that can be explored in this scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T15:17:15-08:00","id":1558221,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't necessarily be clear to them that the God-Machine is bad. ItXers in their ranks might even see the God-Machine as this universe's version of their own Computer, and might even seek to make contact with it.<br /> <br /> The Web of Pain would likely see the Technocrat Construct as a new Conspiracy, a part of itself; and it wouldn't necessarily be wrong: what, really, is the difference between a Deviant and the cyborgs, clones, and other products of Iteration X and the Progenitors?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What will they do when they realize that their methods of manipulating consensus mean nothing because there is no consensus? </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this before; but revisiting it: two boring options to go with would be: Ascension-style Magick continues to work for them as is; or, Ascension-style Magick <i>stops</i> working and they're left powerless. But an interesting middle road might be that their Ascension-style Magick <i>mutates</i>, and gets translated into CoD equivalents. Plural; because even though the most obvious parallel would be the Watchtower Mages, they're not the <i>only</i> parallel. Task Force Valkyrie demonstrates that it's possible to have a Hunter Conspiracy that has access to Hypertech; and as I mentioned above, the enhanced and crafted agents of the Union might as well be Deviants. Heck, a case could even be made for a few agents to effectively become <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eM6TJ-gB0i6FZFL2OXWNaoijDCZW7-Ry7_U-kNtK6X0/edit?tab=t.0\" target=\"_blank\">a new kind of Stigmatic</a>, finding that they can tap into the God-Machine in a manner similar to how the Unchained do.<br /> <br /> Heck, while it's not my cup of tea, the former Enlightened Scientists might even find themselves transformed into <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1324KXmeN8HdOFz4N_zcHeUw_REosiVel\" target=\"_blank\">Geniuses</a> \u2014 possibly the only Geniuses in existence. Seeing as how that fansplat was originally created by former MtAs fans who didn't like that MtAw lacked support for mad scientists, there's a certain appropriateness of Technocrats translating over as Geniuses. (But again, not my cup of tea; see below.)<br /> <br /> So the Hypertech that the Construct brings with it might continue to function even without the Consensus that allowed it to work before the transfer took place; and the Scientists might find that the theories they used as their Focuses before the transfer are actually <i>true</i> in this new reality, allowing them to continue their R&amp;D and the production of more Hypertech; just not through the application of Spheres.<br /> <br /> And yes, a few (some? most? all?) of the formerly Enlightened Scientists might actually Awaken to Watchtowers, or possibly even to <i>new</i> Watchtowers that were created by their arrival in the CoD universe: I have an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e\">Other Five Paths</a> system hack designed to add five new Watchtowers to the setting, and one of the frameworks I've considered for inserting them into the setting is that these new Watchtowers center around the concept of Gifted Science that was introduced in <b>Awakening</b>'s <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b>. I even rescued a &quot;cutting room floor&quot; idea from the authors of the <b>Mage Translation Guide</b>, suggesting that each of my new Watchtowers might be associated with a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161338-mage-translation-guide-the-lost-outtakes?p=1161365#post1161365\">Technocratic Utopia</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Fixing markup 02-26-2026, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T22:25:08-08:00","id":1558224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skyewards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558215#post1558215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The local mages aren\u2019t making life for humanity worse via consensus. They might still dislike them on principle, but it\u2019s not like they\u2019ll be punished by superiors if they team up with ones like the Free Council. Like people have said, the Seers and their Exarchs are the sorts of mages the Technocrats would oppose on principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something very important to make note of, is that the Atlantean Orders are not based on cultural systems like the Mystic Traditions are. Rather, they're a far more organized set of infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <br /> From the Adamantine Arrow serving as the military branch, to the Guardians of the Veil acting as spies and secret police force. Or the Silver Ladder taking on the administrative positions.<br /> <br /> Ascension presented mages in such a way that was pretty much designed for them to be at each other's throats. There's no way that this council is anything more than an alliance of convenience; one that shall tear itself apart once the Technocracy has been finally dealt with.<br /> <br /> While Awakening has presented a means by which multiple Paths are able to cooperate with each other to achieve a common goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T17:21:35-08:00","id":1558515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557383#post1557383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Technocrats wouldn't just be diminished, they'd practically cease to exist, due to how both universes handle the existence of magic. As far as I'm aware, there's no Tower of Technomancy to be found in Awakening.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say they would join on with the Seers of the Throne, as those are probably the closest thing they have to upholding their desired paradigm. But even that would be a bitter pill to swallow, as the world is still under the thumb of godly powerful wizards who control reality.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1. It's not a matter of how magic exists. Magic exists in many ways in each universe, &quot;Mages&quot; have no exclusive claim over magic in either, they have a *specific* type of power that's called &quot;magic&quot; by convenience. What each universe lacks is *the specific metaphysical background* for how the entities we call &quot;Mages&quot; in the other operate;<br /> <br /> 2. The main point is that the characters aren't the same thing. &quot;Mage&quot; is just a convenient shorthand, Ascension and Awakening Mages are different splats altogether, doing different things that follow similar mechanics on game terms for OoC reasons. IC they don't have any similarity;<br /> <br /> 3. Which towers are there is irrelevant. **IF** a Technocrat awakens to a Watchtower it can be to any of them, because Paradigm and belief has zero to do with it. If a Techie awakens to a Watchtower that'll be like a Techie being Embraced or changing into a Werewolf, their new powers and their Paradigm are completely independent matters;<br /> <br /> 4. I see why thinking the Seers look like their paradigm, but they're not in any sense. They have similar methods for completely different goals and radically opposing beliefs, which isn't new to the Union. It's like saying the Technocracy should be buddies with the Camarilla for the same reason;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> ...why would they need to do any of that? An Ascension Mage's magic comes from themselves. They don't need Towers to function. It's not like traveling to other universes is somehow going to turn it off. Especially when Void Engineers do travel to other universes with foreign Umbras.</div> </div> </div> </div> 5. Assuming one setting's metaphysics overwrites the other. There's zero reason to believe that's the case. The power of Ascension Mages isn't *just* internal, it's predicated on how their cosmology works and that's repeated in the books exhaustively;<br /> <br /> 6. Other realms in WoD can and do alter their powers and can overwhelm them completely, this isn't done in official examples just because it's boring, but realms where one or more Spheres either suffer penalties or don't work at all are well documented;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Perhaps the Technocoracy could help the local Mages find better sources of power. If no one needed what the Exarchs monopolize, if the abyss held no power over magic, mages could build utopia in this reality. Remember, Utopia is technically possible in this reality, it's blocked by the Seers and the Exarchs. If the Technocrats could link these mages with their own magic then the Exarchs, the Seers and two points of the Atlantian diamond become irrelevant. More importantly, the Technocrats can liberate themselves and become real heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div> 7. Setting aside other qualms with this, it would heavily contradict Ascension. Reliably Awakening/Illuminating anyone is in itself the Holy Grail of Magick. Since MtAw Mages are **not** MtAs Mages, that would mean reliably Illuminating an entire population. And to other Paradigms nonetheless, which is both weird and of dubious utility;<br /> <br /> 8. This is another world, its inhabitants ***look*** human without any guarantee that they are, and this would give this aliens the power and tools to find and travel to WoD. They may end up the greatest traitors in MtAs history;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Awakening does not have a tellurian, or an Umbra, or a free style approach to magic. It has the Supernal Realms, Watchtowers and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div> 9. Also other phenomena. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> that the most interesting options involve their powers mutating into something CoD-compatible, which is a lot more things than WoD, by the way. I would prefer something minor simply because I like the gritty versions of this plot, but anything is possible. That said yeah, that's the gist of it;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Willworking uses different metaphysics, but not necessarily incompatible with the overall metaphysics of the CoD setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> 10. With a caveat: if the *Consensus* is real *and* CoD humans are really humans for WoD standards, then we have strong (not overwhelming) evidence it is incompatible;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Tellurian is a thing, and the shadow also exists</div> </div> </div> </div> 11. The Tellurian is a theoretical framework with no meaning of its own, and the Shadow from CoD is a completely distinct thing from WoD's Umbra. This literally means nothing;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skyewards</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> They still have their mission to protect humanity, especially if they\u2019re the idealistic type.</div> </div> </div> </div> 12. **IF** they assume those are real humans. This is another world, and human-like aliens aren't unknown to the Union. CoD humans have few but relevant differences from WoD, including a wildly different standard reaction to supernatural beings. While we don't know the reason, the Technocrats have no reason to believe their mission apply to those people;<br /> <br /> 13. The Web of Pain is an analytical category, not a formal organization. The conspiracies are independent, do not know much about each other, do not know about everything in the world. Overall this Union is coming to a world where their M.O. is far from unique, or even rare;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Heck, while it's not my cup of tea, the former Enlightened Scientists might even find themselves transformed into Geniuses \u2014 possibly the only Geniuses in existence.</div> </div> </div> </div> 14. If the ST uses Genius, I'd say this, not MtAw, is the closest to MtAs you'll find in CoD, and unavoidably the best option for Technocrats, not only for the technology approach, but for their relationship with the concept of Paradigm;<br /> <br /> 15. CoD being CoD, their tech could still work even with them not becoming anything other than normal human all by itself. It could work as Atlantean artifacts, items from almost any splat, or just be genuinely the real deal. Let's remember that Valkyrie doesn't just have hyper-tech, as far as we know it's indeed just tech;<br /> <br /> 16. Weird interesting option? Their arrival could create/reveal new Watchtowers not for them, but for other new Mages. You could have the Techies getting no or regular CoD powers, to later find out their coming triggered changes around the world;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Ascension presented mages in such a way that was pretty much designed for them to be at each other's throats. There's no way that this council is anything more than an alliance of convenience; one that shall tear itself apart once the Technocracy has been finally dealt with.<br /> <br /> While Awakening has presented a means by which multiple Paths are able to cooperate with each other to achieve a common goal.</div> </div> </div> </div> 17. I've talked earlier in the thread about how the settings work very differently in many ways beyond just powers. It has a very distinct approach to how supernatural societies work because WoD is designed for conflict and paranoia as default. All societies are in some level spy agencies locked in a global cold war with at least a few others and lots of hidden proxies. CoD is meant for local arrangements and politics, and direct relationships more important than generalizations, even at global scales.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T18:04:49-08:00","id":1558517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 17. I've talked earlier in the thread about how the settings work very differently in many ways beyond just powers. It has a very distinct approach to how supernatural societies work because WoD is designed for conflict and paranoia as default. All societies are in some level spy agencies locked in a global cold war with at least a few others and lots of hidden proxies. CoD is meant for local arrangements and politics, and direct relationships more important than generalizations, even at global scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Atlantean Orders, you have mages organized into societal roles. Administration, military, police force, est.<br /> <br /> With the Mystic Traditions, you have mages organized into wildly different cultures and belief systems. <br /> <br /> A coven of nature worshipers, who wish to protect the natural world + a university of steam punk pseudo-scientists, that want to turn the world into a Rocket Man painting + a cabal of death honoring assassins simply is not compatible with each other in the long term. Eventually, something is going to push them into conflict, and it's only due to the fact they have a common enemy to focus on that keeps them distracted from that fact.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T18:16:12-08:00","id":1558518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557725#post1557725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which now that I think about it, is a bit confusing. If the Exarchs don't want people to awaken to magic, and they are currently the rulers of the Supernal realms, why don't they simply destroy the towers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a question that could be answered on the Awakening forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1557736#post1557736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E604uxkVqhk\" data-code=\"E604uxkVqhk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/E604uxkVqhk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I would keep in mind that trailer is about twenty years old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T23:06:22-08:00","id":1558523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. It's not a matter of how magic exists. Magic exists in many ways in each universe, &quot;Mages&quot; have no exclusive claim over magic in either, they have a *specific* type of power that's called &quot;magic&quot; by convenience. What each universe lacks is *the specific metaphysical background* for how the entities we call &quot;Mages&quot; in the other operate;<br /> <br /> 2. The main point is that the characters aren't the same thing. &quot;Mage&quot; is just a convenient shorthand, Ascension and Awakening Mages are different splats altogether, doing different things that follow similar mechanics on game terms for OoC reasons. IC they don't have any similarity;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to make a comment about how the God Machine might get involved, once it heard about the alleged source of their Awakened Avatars. But then I remembered the splats in CoD are self contained unless the Storyteller decides otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. Which towers are there is irrelevant. **IF** a Technocrat awakens to a Watchtower it can be to any of them, because Paradigm and belief has zero to do with it. If a Techie awakens to a Watchtower that'll be like a Techie being Embraced or changing into a Werewolf, their new powers and their Paradigm are completely independent matters;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's relevant in the sense that the Technocracy don't want you to believe in the existence of magic. They want you to believe in science, in rationality, in things which can be easily quantified and explained. Drawing power from the realm of Fey, Demons, Gods, Ghosts and Spirits flies in the face of everything they stand for.<br /> <br /> To circumvent this, they would have to imitate the Emperor of Mankind, and try to build some kind of giant wall to keep the denizens of those realms from interacting with mortals, while simultaneously having access to the power those realms provide. But we can just take a look at the story of Magnus the Red, to teach us that remaining ignorant of the encroaching threat is never a good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. I see why thinking the Seers look like their paradigm, but they're not in any sense. They have similar methods for completely different goals and radically opposing beliefs, which isn't new to the Union. It's like saying the Technocracy should be buddies with the Camarilla for the same reason;<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Technocracy don't want you to believe in magic. They want you to believe in established laws of science and nature. Likewise, the Exarchs want the sleepers to stay sleepers, and believe that the laws of the universe are fixed and immutable.<br /> <br /> So, again, supporting the Seers is the closest option they have to establishing their desired paradigm. Assuming that the Exarchs don't suddenly decide to change the rules one day, should the mood strike them.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T00:22:47-08:00","id":1558524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. With a caveat: if the *Consensus* is real *and* CoD humans are really humans for WoD standards, then we have strong (not overwhelming) evidence it is incompatible;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200bFair enough. In particular, that wouldn't necessarily mean that a Technocrat engaging in willworking would fail; because in general, that doesn't involve the Consensus except in the sense of &quot;reality pushes back against your willworking&quot;. But if the Technocrats attempt to engage in any Terranorming, then <i>that </i>might very well fail outright. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13. The Web of Pain is an analytical category, not a formal organization. The conspiracies are independent, do not know much about each other, do not know about everything in the world. Overall this Union is coming to a world where their M.O. is far from unique, or even rare;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026which is why I suggested the possibility that the Technocratic Construct might end up being another Conspiracy in the Web of Pain. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">14. If the ST uses Genius, I'd say this, not MtAw, is the closest to MtAs you'll find in CoD, and unavoidably the best option for Technocrats, not only for the technology approach, but for their relationship with the concept of Paradigm;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still fail myself with Genius; but from what I understand of its origins, this isn't a coincidence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">15. CoD being CoD, their tech could still work even with them not becoming anything other than normal human all by itself. It could work as Atlantean artifacts, items from almost any splat, or just be genuinely the real deal. Let's remember that Valkyrie doesn't just have hyper-tech, as far as we know it's indeed just tech;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;just tech&quot; is indeed part of the point: the nature of the CoD setting includes what I'd call &quot;occult tech&quot;. <br /> <br /> CoD gamelines that would be most suitable for interacting with the Technocracy would be: <br /> <br /> <b><u>Mage: the Awakening</u></b><br /> Not for the Magic, but for the business about Obsessions and investigation of supernatural phenomena. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Promethean: the Created</u></b><br /> I'm thinking primarily of the Unfleshed here. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Hunter: the Vigil</u></b><br /> As Task Force Valkyrie demonstrates, a Hunter Conspiracy can feature Hypertech. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Demon: the Descent</u></b><br /> Techgnostic espionage; 'nuff said. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Deviant: the Renegades</u></b><br /> Hybrids and Cyborgs in particular are appropriate for Technocrat-focused games; but Psychics aren't far behind. <br /> <br /> If you want to fit Technocrats entirely into existing CoD structures, I'd primarily use a mix of Mage (for talented inventor types), Hunter (for human agents with not-so-mundane gear), and Deviant (for inhuman agents manufactured by the Construct). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">16. Weird interesting option? Their arrival could create/reveal new Watchtowers not for them, but for other new Mages. You could have the Techies getting no or regular CoD powers, to later find out their coming triggered changes around the world;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026either as an extension of their nature (i.e., bringing in more tech-themed Darkness to the setting) or as an oppositional reaction to it. In this vein, there's a STV sourcebook for Demon: the Descent that strives to remove the religious overtones of the game and to instead lean into the espionage angle: instead of the God-Machine and its Angels, you get the Machine and its Agents, for example. The arrival of the Technocratic Construct might trigger an Outbreak of the Contagion, remaking the local God-Machine in this way. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T02:52:53-08:00","id":1558525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558515#post1558515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 15. CoD being CoD, their tech could still work even with them not becoming anything other than normal human all by itself. It could work as Atlantean artifacts, items from almost any splat, or just be genuinely the real deal. Let's remember that Valkyrie doesn't just have hyper-tech, as far as we know it's indeed just tech;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the opposite, since it seems to be a pretty established bit of lore that the hyper tech does not work for normal people, specifically because of how radically advanced it is. The sleepers just can't wrap their heads around how it's supposed to work.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Energy swords that produce a super conductive loop of plasma that can maintain its structural integrity outside of a containment unit.<br /> <br /> Singularity rifles that fire miniature black holes without destroying the very weapon from the inside out, and you along with it.<br /> <br /> Vessels capable of traveling faster than the speed of light, despite all known laws of physics telling us that such a feat is impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T08:46:07-08:00","id":1558528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558524#post1558524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still fail myself with Genius; but from what I understand of its origins, this isn't a coincidence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. In addition to everything else it is, Genius is also a satire of MtAsc done, in my opinion, with a lot of heart. I actually really like it as a fan game and I think it could be put to good use here. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T04:37:57-07:00","id":1562252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1558525#post1558525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue the opposite, since it seems to be a pretty established bit of lore that the hyper tech does not work for normal people, specifically because of how radically advanced it is. The sleepers just can't wrap their heads around how it's supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not lore, it's the Union's theory to explain why only they can reliably use Devices and only they can use hypertech Instruments. With the actual reason being those things should not work at all, they do because Mages.<br /> <br /> Same as each Tradition has theories on how and why their practice work, they have theories on why and how Sleepers can't replicate their effects, those just don't get a lot of wordcount. But they're corollaries to the first.<br /> <br /> For the Hermetics since Magic is an act of Will, you need an exceptional Will to make it. They don't know Willpower exist as a trait and that a Sleeper with Willpower 10 is still not a Mage while a Mage with starting Willpower still hasn't Willpower 10.<br /> <br /> Does Magic comes from piercing the lie of Maya? Then Sleepers can't pierce it even if they meditate and practice Do. From liberating your mind? Sleepers are still too attached. Being of the right lucidity to judge the Wheel? Sleepers have clogged judgment.<br /> <br /> Every theory on how one's Magic works carries the explanation of why Sleepers can't replicate it. Few really believe in the &quot;we're supernatural beings, they're not&quot; explanation as the end of it.<br /> <br /> It so happens that the Technocracy believes in their tech. The belief that they're working within the Consensus brings with itself the belief that they're not using their Enlightenment to break the rules of reality determined by the Masses, they're using extremely advanced hypertech to explore the limits and loopholes of this reality. It so happens that this is so advanced that it takes a Genius to operate such complicated prototypes.<br /> <br /> But on transportation to CoD, the metaphysics of this new world kicks in, and the setting can change their Devices and Instruments in any way. So yes, it can make them just work with a little examination and correct procedures. It is not that complicated unless this reality says so.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you decide for your canon that the Union is actually objectively right, has been right all the time, and they're a different and more reliable thing than superstitionists, with their tech being superior to Magic. Then sure, it could really be intrinsically complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T07:20:15-07:00","id":1562258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562252#post1562252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not lore, it's the Union's theory to explain why only they can reliably use Devices and only they can use hypertech Instruments. With the actual reason being those things should not work at all, they do because Mages.<br /> <br /> Same as each Tradition has theories on how and why their practice work, they have theories on why and how Sleepers can't replicate their effects, those just don't get a lot of wordcount. But they're corollaries to the first.<br /> <br /> For the Hermetics since Magic is an act of Will, you need an exceptional Will to make it. They don't know Willpower exist as a trait and that a Sleeper with Willpower 10 is still not a Mage while a Mage with starting Willpower still hasn't Willpower 10.<br /> <br /> Does Magic comes from piercing the lie of Maya? Then Sleepers can't pierce it even if they meditate and practice Do. From liberating your mind? Sleepers are still too attached. Being of the right lucidity to judge the Wheel? Sleepers have clogged judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Took me a few moments, but I think I understand the gist of what you're saying.<br /> <br /> The whole 'super genius' excuse is the Technocracy's coping mechanism for Sleepers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562252#post1562252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It so happens that the Technocracy believes in their tech. The belief that they're working within the Consensus brings with itself the belief that they're not using their Enlightenment to break the rules of reality determined by the Masses, they're using extremely advanced hypertech to explore the limits and loopholes of this reality. <b>It so happens that this is so advanced that it takes a Genius to operate such complicated prototypes.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what <i>'user manuals'</i> are for.<br /> <br /> Remember the Consensus experiment about how most Sleepers wouldn't actually be able to explain to you WHY an air plane is capable of flight. They might give you a mechanical breakdown of how the plane is assembled, and how it interacts with physics. But they couldn't tell you why those things work the way that they do. They simply accept it in their minds, and thus the plane stays airborne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T10:51:12-07:00","id":1562265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562258#post1562258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Took me a few moments, but I think I understand the gist of what you're saying.<br /> <br /> The whole 'super genius' excuse is the Technocracy's coping mechanism for Sleepers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's what <i>'user manuals'</i> are for.<br /> <br /> Remember the Consensus experiment about how most Sleepers wouldn't actually be able to explain to you WHY an air plane is capable of flight. They might give you a mechanical breakdown of how the plane is assembled, and how it interacts with physics. But they couldn't tell you why those things work the way that they do. They simply accept it in their minds, and thus the plane stays airborne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you got it.<br /> <br /> Sleepers can't use Technocratic stuff because they're Sleepers, and the stuff in question was made by and for Mages with a technomantic Paradigm.<br /> <br /> A typical Technocratic Plasma Canon isn't an actual, functional Plasma Canon, otherwise an user manual would do the trick. It is just an Instrument that work because the operator has Arete, Prime and Forces.<br /> <br /> Outside the ambiguity shenanigans from Mage that are vital to the game, but fundamentally an Agent of the Union is a Technomancer that don't like the title. Their stuff work because it's Magic, and only Mages operate Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T15:46:46-07:00","id":1562385,"title":"","content":"I would add that the Union has a f few tricks at its disposal to blur the lines between \u201cwhat Enlightened Scientists can do\u201d and \u201cwhat the Masses can do\u201d: <br /> <br /> 1. Devices that feature Adjustments (Coincidental Effects) can be used by anyone who accepts the general Focus; and as the opening paragraphs concerning Technocratic Reality Zones in M20 point out, that's practically everyone where Technocratic Reality is concerned. Note that the first part of the \u201cTechnocratic Reality Zone\u201d entry in M20 points out that Enlightened Science has the Coincidental Edge \u2014 meaning that a number of Effects that would be considered Vulgar if performed by others are considered Coincidental when performed using Technocratic Practices. <br /> <br /> 2. Devices that feature Procedures (Vulgar Effects) can be used by Extraordinary Citizens. Extraordinary Citizens are a subset of the Masses, and it's somewhat unclear where the line between \u201cOrdinary Citizens\u201d and \u201cExtraordinary Citizens\u201d lies, in-setting; but it appears to have something to do with how steeped they are in the metaphysics: it could be argued that Extraordinary Citizens are individuals with enough Enlightened Will to have a Focus the way Enlightened Scientists do, even of they lack the discernable Genius and Enlightenment that Enlightened Scientists display. (Terminology is a little muddy here, as \u201cEnlightenment\u201d \u2014 the term Technocrats use as a substitute for \u201cArete\u201d \u2014 isn't the same as the \u201cEnlightened\u201d part of \u201cEnlightened Will\u201d for this purpose.)<br /> <br /> 3. A Technocrat using Management and Human Resources can work an Adjustment <i>through the activities of a team of Ordinary Citizens</i>. The Scientist needs to be directing the activities (though not necessarily micromanaging it); but the people being directed, or outsiders observing them, could easily come to the conclusion that <i>they're</i> the ones working the Effect, through their teamwork. And again, there's the Coincidental Edge, making a wider range of Effects count as Adjustments that thus can be performed through Management and Human Resources. <br /> <br /> 4. Extraordinary Citizens can also learn techno-sorcery, picking up Paths that let them work the equivalent of individual Effects without needing Devices or the direction of Enlightened Scientists to make it possible. And recall that the line between \u201cOrdinary Citizen\u201d and \u201cExtraordinary Citizen\u201d is blurry. <br /> <br /> Of course, this is <i>mainly</i> most relevant in the World of Darkness. As mentioned above, there's a very real possibility that the metaphysics of Magick simply don't work in the Chronicles of Darkness, rendering this whole issue moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T19:39:03-07:00","id":1562394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562385#post1562385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that the Union has a f few tricks at its disposal to blur the lines between \u201cwhat Enlightened Scientists can do\u201d and \u201cwhat the Masses can do\u201d:</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but in the end those tricks reinforce the fundamental ambiguity/error of the notion that their tech is just too complicated. Using your numbers:<br /> <br /> 1. That means an equally smart person can't use the Device if they don't strictly accept the Focus. Likely any engineer that examines the Device and concludes it shouldn't work, because their focus is <b>not</b> regular science. Also an individual that regularly uses the Device in the right Reality Zone somehow can't elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Union knows and has theories to explain both. But they still contradict the idea that Enlightenment is just a lot of smarts.<br /> <br /> 2. Extraordinary Citizens are individually more reliable, but they clearly rely more on loyalty and buy in than smarts, which is another problem to the thesis. You don't need to believe something works to operate it correctly, but you need to have whatever technical knowledge it requires.<br /> <br /> Reality Zone users of Coincidental Devices at least have to actually understand and operate the Device because that's how it works to them. With Extraordinary Citizens things are less clear cut. Sure, they're usually well trained, but just how well each of them really got it?<br /> <br /> 3. Love Management as Instrument, but it will bring a similar situation: anyone can use this tech <i>as long as they have the right boss</i>. And no, this boss isn't giving technical instructions, they're occupied with a nouveau set of kanban boards for Advanced Scrum System 7.5.<br /> <br /> 4. Techno-sorcerers only make them even more similar to the Traditions, as they need this quasi-esoteric studies program just to be able to use certain Instruments. <hr /><br /> And the best part of all: some of those too-hard-for-inferior-minds Instruments just require that you press a button.<br /> <br /> Granted, not all of them. But enough of them.<br /> <br /> Hence why in CoD (or any other world, including possibly umbral realms) it is possible that an Instrument or Device will &quot;become real&quot; and just work for anyone who read the manual or fiddle enough to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T16:03:42-07:00","id":1562447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, but in the end those tricks reinforce the fundamental ambiguity/error of the notion that their tech is just too complicated. Using your numbers:<br /> <br /> 1. That means an equally smart person can't use the Device if they don't strictly accept the Focus. Likely any engineer that examines the Device and concludes it shouldn't work, because their focus is <b>not</b> regular science. Also an individual that regularly uses the Device in the right Reality Zone somehow can't elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just need to push back on this a little bit. The first paragraph under Technocratic Reality in M20 says that their stuff gets the Coincidental edge because \u201cscience-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.\u201d I submit that Coincidental Technocratic stuff, at least, <i>wouldn't </i>cause a regular engineer to conclude it shouldn't work. A Device that produces a <i>Vulgar </i>Effect, sure; but the Coincidental stuff is arguably a different story. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Extraordinary Citizens are individually more reliable, but they clearly rely more on loyalty and buy in than smarts, which is another problem to the thesis. You don't need to believe something works to operate it correctly, but you need to have whatever technical knowledge it requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite so sure that's as clear a distinction as you might think. Sure, to a mystical mage, \u201cbuy in\u201d translates to \u201cbelief\u201d; but to a Technocrat, \u201cbuy in\u201d translates to \u201cthey're not nuts\u201d. Believing that technology works just means that you're not a raging loon, like those Superstitionists. <br /> <br /> There's a guy I've run across on YouTube who defends Intelligent Design. If you check his credentials, he's <i>incredibly </i>smart. But as smart as he is, he rejects the theory of evolution. He says that it's because the evidence doesn't add up. In terms of what we're discussing, he has plenty of smarts but (on the theory of evolution), no buy in. <br /> <br /> Put another way, \u201call you need is to be smart\u201d isn't true; even in the real world, it's more important that you have at least a minimal buy in (as in, not believe insane conspiracy theories) than it is to be smart. <br /> <br /> And again, note that the <i>second </i>paragraph under Technocratic Reality points out that virtually everybody, even the mystics of the Nine Traditions, has \u201cbuy in\u201d to much of Technocratic Reality. Finding someone who <i>doesn't </i>believe that \u201cwhen you press a button, things happen\u201d is <i>incredibly </i>rare. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reality Zone users of Coincidental Devices at least have to actually understand and operate the Device because that's how it works to them. With Extraordinary Citizens things are less clear cut. Sure, they're usually well trained, but just how well each of them really got it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how important it is for a Reality Zone user of Coincidental Devices to understand them. Most people don't know how a radio works; they only know <i>that </i>it works. Extraordinary Citizens, by contrast, are generally the sorts of folks who are familiar enough with the Technocracy's Focus that they likely <i>do </i>understand it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Love Management as Instrument, but it will bring a similar situation: anyone can use this tech <i>as long as they have the right boss</i>. And no, this boss isn't giving technical instructions, they're occupied with a nouveau set of kanban boards for Advanced Scrum System 7.5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entry on Management and Human Resources in M20 specifically and repeatedly points out that direction by the manager is an essential feature of this Instrument; there's nothing about them being \u201coccupied by a set of kanban boards for Advanced Scrum System 7.5\u201d, whatever that means. <br /> <br /> And yeah, it <i>does </i>only work if they have the right boss. But unless you're specifically trying to explain how it's actually a Magickal Instrument and not just a talented boss who knows how to get the most out of his team, that doesn't change the fact that a team of Ordinary Citizens is performing an Adjustment. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Techno-sorcerers only make them even more similar to the Traditions, as they need this quasi-esoteric studies program just to be able to use certain Instruments.</div> </div> </div> </div>But <i>are </i>they esoteric studies programs? Exactly how are you supposed to draw the line between an ordinary engineer and an Extraordinary Engineer? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the best part of all: some of those too-hard-for-inferior-minds Instruments just require that you press a button.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll note that in <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, every Procedure and Adjustment is paired with a Device. A case could be made that the \u201cjust press a button Instruments\u201d are, in fact, Devices. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562394#post1562394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence why in CoD (or any other world, including possibly umbral realms) it is possible that an Instrument or Device will &quot;become real&quot; and just work for anyone who read the manual or fiddle enough to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not arguing against that. But would anyone notice? My point is that there's already enough ambiguity that most if not all Technocratic stuff already appears to work that way. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T23:26:11-07:00","id":1562457,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, my points are:<br /> <br /> 1. A piece of technology &quot;really works&quot; when it only requires the correct action. Understanding or buy in aren't necessary to operate it. We can summarize a test as:<ul><li>The right set of actions performed in the right conditions will work</li> <li>Knowledge isn't required</li> <li>Belief isn't required</li> <li>Knowledge is possible without belief</li> <li>Belief is possible without knowledge</li> <li>If operation is highly complex, technical qualification can be required</li> <li>Technical qualification can be objective and independently tested</li> </ul><br /> 2. The theory of &quot;Mages are just really smart&quot; (which isn't exclusive to the Union or universal in the Union, it's just their party line) demand that their creations (Devices or Instruments) &quot;really work&quot;. It doesn't mean there can't be pieces whose operation really is that complex, but at some level they'd really work.<br /> <br /> 3. Since the premises of the setting break falsifiability, neither side can ultimately prove the other wrong, I'm only pointing evidence with a certain weight. But still an exception has greater statistical weight than confirmation by the principle of Occam's Razor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just need to push back on this a little bit. The first paragraph under Technocratic Reality in M20 says that their stuff gets the Coincidental edge because \u201cscience-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.\u201d I submit that Coincidental Technocratic stuff, at least, <i>wouldn't </i>cause a regular engineer to conclude it shouldn't work. A Device that produces a <i>Vulgar </i>Effect, sure; but the Coincidental stuff is arguably a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that we're not talking either the Omniscient Observer nor the Casual Observer, but something fundamentally different: a Specialized Examiner. An engineer can explore the device to reach their own conclusions based on their specific knowledge.<br /> <br /> Likewise, we're not talking belief in General Principles, but belief in This Item. Given what the engineer knows and can do, their buy in doesn't follow from mere theory.<br /> <br /> Example: a Technocratic laser works on well accepted general principles an engineer wouldn't question. But if you give one the laser and its blueprint, the engineer will actually be able to analyze it and verify if it is well crafted according to known tech, and calculate its output.<br /> <br /> Here general principles fail. The engineer isn't being required to believe in science or in laser technology, but that this particular equipment is capable, from its specific configuration, to execute the exact functions it has.<br /> <br /> And since we're talking &quot;over the edge&quot; tech, it isn't a given. You're essentially leaving the area where all scientists agree for the realm where scientists can violently disagree. An engineer can, at this point, totally conclude it shouldn't work for purely technical or theoretical reasons<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite so sure that's as clear a distinction as you might think. Sure, to a mystical mage, \u201cbuy in\u201d translates to \u201cbelief\u201d; but to a Technocrat, \u201cbuy in\u201d translates to \u201cthey're not nuts\u201d. Believing that technology works just means that you're not a raging loon, like those Superstitionists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is actually reinforced, because the problem isn't that Extraordinary Citizens have to believe. It's that they must be Extraordinary Citizens.<br /> <br /> As fuzzy as the distinction between them and regular people may be, it objectively exists. So while the existence of Extraordinary Citizens makes it arguable that Technocratic tech does not require a Technocrat, the fact that most citizens are not Extraordinary Citizens means a distinction still exists.<br /> <br /> If the thesis is true, the difference between an Extraordinary Citizen and a regular person will be technical qualification. If it is not, then we have a hole. And so happens by the book that the difference seems to mostly be loyalty and how deep the buy in is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how important it is for a Reality Zone user of Coincidental Devices to understand them. Most people don't know how a radio works; they only know <i>that </i>it works. Extraordinary Citizens, by contrast, are generally the sorts of folks who are familiar enough with the Technocracy's Focus that they likely <i>do </i>understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me neither, but the Union thinks it is.<br /> <br /> What I meant is that within their Reality Zone the Union can demonstrate their thesis. If their technology just requires understanding, within the Reality Zone this is demonstrable.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary Citizens don't have the same weight because they can be utterly ignorant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entry on Management and Human Resources in M20 specifically and repeatedly points out that direction by the manager is an essential feature of this Instrument; there's nothing about them being \u201coccupied by a set of kanban boards for Advanced Scrum System 7.5\u201d, whatever that means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means direction by the manager, literally.<br /> <br /> A manager doesn't give technical instructions on equipment operation. They organize worker teams activities. Kanban and Scrum are two well known management systems, the kind of thing a Scientific Manager would study, apply and improve.<br /> <br /> So the problem here is: the people under their management are able to use Union tech while under supervision, but not without it. But they operate the tech in the same way, management only covers their actions in a higher order. Why can't they use that Union laser except when the boss is telling them to use it and where?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>are </i>they esoteric studies programs? Exactly how are you supposed to draw the line between an ordinary engineer and an Extraordinary Engineer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't need to draw the line, just to see that it exists somewhere.<br /> <br /> For clarification: I know their main difference is the Sorcerer actually making incredible stuff and I'm not arguing that. This would indeed be impossible to say. My focus is the ability to use Union tech.<br /> <br /> Here the problem is again a need of knowledge where technical qualification should be enough to work. Saying the engineer that underwent the super duper study program makes things that are extraordinary is ok. Saying the regular engineer isn't even capable of operating the equipment is a huge stretch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that in <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, every Procedure and Adjustment is paired with a Device. A case could be made that the \u201cjust press a button Instruments\u201d are, in fact, Devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could, but isn't implied by basic rules. Unless you house rule that Instruments have to require complex processes to qualify, all it takes is a PC declaring their Instrument is simpler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not arguing against that. But would anyone notice? My point is that there's already enough ambiguity that most if not all Technocratic stuff already appears to work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would for an important reason: lost stuff.<br /> <br /> Agents loose equipment in mission, an old or lost Construct is sacked, or any of a series of possible events end up with Technocratic stuff in the hands of others.<br /> <br /> In WoD this is of little relevance. While the Union will do everything they can to recover or destroy the item, the fact remains that it can't be used or reproduced by others even without safety protocols.<br /> <br /> But in other realities, if they really work, they can, and safety protocols are more likely to fail. Imagine Task Force Valkyrie putting their hands in such artifacts. Or the Lucifuge. Those ate perfectly possible scenarios.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T01:45:12-07:00","id":1562461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562447#post1562447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A case could be made that the \u201cjust press a button Instruments\u201d are, in fact, Devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wondered about that for years. That always felt like the obvious conclusion, but not something that the books would ever actually say explicitly (least not that I've seen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T02:04:20-07:00","id":1562462,"title":"","content":"To probably no one's surprise, Mage actually isn't clear about the exact nature of an Extraordinary Citizen. You speak about them as if that was a metaphysically distinct category; but is it? <br /> <br /> What's the difference between a hedge magician (such as those described in <b>Hunters Hunted 2</b>) and a sorcerer (as described in the various <b>Sorcerer</b> books)? The former are described as perfectly ordinary people who have stumbled across a bit of magic that they don't really understand; the latter are sometimes described as being somehow vaguely set apart from ordinary people. Especially after <b>Sorcerer Revised</b> added mechanical complexity in the form of Aspects to its Paths, it might be possible to argue that <b>HH2</b> hedge magicians and sorcerers are two different things, practicing two similar but distinct arts that just do happen to resemble each other, and that hedge wizardry is something that anyone can pick up whereas sorcery is only available to a select few who have some undefinable quality that lets them use it. But it's equally possible that hedge wizardry and sorcery are the same thing; that the hedge wizardry of <b>HH2</b> is a subset of the sorcery of <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> that preselects a Focus (along essentially Hermetic lines) and makes assumptions about how the Paths will be used; assumptions that <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> doesn't make. If so, then either the hedge magicians of <b>HH2</b> are unknowingly special, or the sorcerers of <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> <i>aren't </i>special. <br /> <br /> I mentioned before that, in my view, an Extraordinary Citizen has a Focus while an \u201cOrdinary Citizen\u201d doesn't. But while that might sound like a sharp distinction, it may actually just be a difference of degree rather than a difference of type. How do we know that your Specialized Examiner doesn't qualify as an Extraordinary Citizen by virtue of <i>being </i>a Specialized Examiner? Maybe the technical know-how that your engineer has <i>defines</i> a Focus; so, far from being a neutral observer who can objectively draw a line between science and techno-sorcery, by virtue of <i>being</i> an engineer he is definitionally already an Extraordinary Citizen. Techno-sorcery is merely a game construct for representing an Extraordinary Citizen who has learned a few secrets that are ahead of his time. And anyone who puts in the effort to learn that stuff will end up becoming a techno-sorcerer too (or perhaps the \u201chedge magician\u201d counterpart to a techno-sorcerer).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T03:40:43-07:00","id":1562469,"title":"","content":"A) A talisman (definitely not the word a member of the Technocratic Union would use) could have non Magic functions. Picture a Smart Phone that is a talisman. It is fully functional as a phone and access to the internet and wasting time with video games and YouTube. It also has some special apps. <br /> <br /> B) There are minor magics that the Hermetics teach that allow just about anyone to do small magics, very small. It seems likely that the Technocratic Union would have a few things that are just beyond the bleeding edge by a micron or two that are basically the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T05:28:09-07:00","id":1562475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562462#post1562462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To probably no one's surprise, Mage actually isn't clear about the exact nature of an Extraordinary Citizen. You speak about them as if that was a metaphysically distinct category; but is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not and was abundantly clear about it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562457#post1562457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Since the premises of the setting break falsifiability, <i><b>neither side can ultimately prove the other wrong</b></i>, I'm only pointing evidence with a certain weight. But still an exception has greater statistical weight than confirmation by the principle of Occam's Razor.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <i><b>As fuzzy as the distinction between them and regular people may be</b></i>, it objectively exists. So while the existence of Extraordinary Citizens makes it arguable that Technocratic tech does not require a Technocrat, <b><i>the fact that most citizens are not Extraordinary Citizens means a distinction still exists.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>You're twisting my words when you point to possible explanations as if I didn't recognize they're there.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary Citizens can be whatever the ST want them to be, if they even want to define it, without breaking with canon, that's the goal. That's in the whole &quot;ambiguity is fundamental to Mage&quot; part I said earlier, and was just talking about why Technocratic spiel isn't what it says, unless the ST decides it is.<br /> <br /> Or, more precisely, <i><b>I'm talking about why the ST can make the Technocracy wrong if they want</b></i>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm aware of at least 3 or 4 ways of working out Extraordinary Citizens so they're perfectly normal people. It just so happens that they require more extra assumptions about the setting than many ways of making them special.<br /> <br /> My point: <i><b>whatever Extraordinary Citizens are, it is not the same as ordinary</b></i> people. Period. Not saying this is metaphysical.<br /> <br /> The difference can be training. Knowledge. To be in a database of authorized users. Union tech may actually have a standard safety key and Agents are not authorized to make Devices or Instruments without it. Is the ST required by the setting to pick one? Or is the setting made to not assume this unless the ST wants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T06:48:46-07:00","id":1562477,"title":"","content":"I will note then, as my final statement here, that I never twisted your words \u2014 phrasing that carries a connotation of deceptiveness and/or ill intent. I disagreed with you, and tried to point out where I thought you were mistaken. But I never tried to misrepresent what you were saying, and I'm a bit offended that you thought that I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:24:28-07:00","id":1562484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540876-how-would-the-technocrat-react-to-the-chronicle-of-darkness?p=1562477#post1562477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note then, as my final statement here, that I never twisted your words \u2014 phrasing that carries a connotation of deceptiveness and/or ill intent. I disagreed with you, and tried to point out where I thought you were mistaken. But I never tried to misrepresent what you were saying, and I'm a bit offended that you thought that I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I've been irritated lately and went overboard, felt offended without much reason. Even then, offending was not the intention.<br /> <br /> And I do not really disagree with you, I was just talking how it is not automatically in favor of a &quot;pro-Technocracy&quot; interpretation, and may have let myself carry by that.<br /> <br /> But yes, the game is, after all, made for truth to be absolutely uncertain, and that does mean it is completely feasible that the Union is actually right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}